{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing","id":1051116,"title":"Okay, so let's read this thing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-18T13:07:36-08:00","id":1051116,"title":"Okay, so let's read this thing","content":"During some slow times at work today I browsed the forums and got a sudden urge to try out a new game. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1050908-i-want-to-get-into-this-game\">I made a thread asking questions about <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></a> and ended up purchasing the <b>Corebook</b> as well as <b>Hurt Locker</b> both as PDFs and as premium edition prints on demand. As work kept being slow, the replies in that other thread made me recognize that the preconceptions I had about the game were vastly different from what it actually is.<br /> <br /> I've known about the World of Darkness for a very long time. But knowing about it is pretty much it. I think I played a session of <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> a decade ago and I've played a few sessions of <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b>. I've browsed a friend's <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> book without actually absorbing any of its content. Since my main game for the last decade has been <b>Exalted</b>, I've assumed that the WoD splats have been similar to the splats in that game; seamlessly part of the same setting and built off the same mechanics. I assumed that World of Darkness encouraged mixed groups just like Exalted did, and it was first now after creating that thread (on the same day as I actually bought my first Chronicles of Darkness products) that I recognized that the gamelines are vastly different in that regard. I understand now that the various splats exist in a unified setting, but as individual games. There is no such thing as a seamless transition. The games are different. The mythos is the same.<br /> <br /> And what the hell is a <b>God Machine Chronicle</b>? Don't tell me yet.<br /> <br /> I will be reading Chronicles of Darkness in this thread. As of me writing this I haven't started yet. I am going to give my honest impressions on what I read, based on my own personal interests as well as the games I'm familiar with. I expect that there will be a lot of comparisons to Exalted since that's the game I'm most familiar with. I will also ask questions that arise as I read, and hopefully learn more about the game from the discussions that may come about in this thread. I will try to focus on a chapter at the time and I would encourage anyone who wants to reply to this thread to keep it from digressing too much.<br /> <br /> I have set the mood to be able to get into this: the Chronicles of Darkness PDF on Monitor 1, the document where I'm writing this and where I'm taking notes on Monitor 2, and a World of Darkness-inspired music list as well as a Skype window on Monitor 3. I have mood lighting, scented candles and coffee. <b>Now let's get started!</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>COVER</b><br /> <br /> The cover, depicting a blurry individual in a blurry environment with a blue hue, doesn't really grab my attention. I understand that it goes for mood, with the blur effects symbolizing another world overlaying reality. It feels a bit easy, though, and a bit boring. The logo is cool. I like the font and it grabs my attention much more than the actual picture.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>INTRO FICTION: \u201cAPT, 3B\u201d BY AUDREY WHITMAN</b><br /> <br /> This intro fiction is the first thing I'm reading from the Chronicles of Darkness. It's a decent story. I don't really have many problems with it, apart from a few pet peeves. The fiction is very dialogue heavy, and it focuses on the interaction between the characters more than setting a scene. I understand that it's trying to set up a scene through dialogue---but that's telling. I want to <i>be shown</i> the scene. I want to get in the mood. The characters aren't displaying much emotion before the \u201c<b>And then ...</b>\u201d part. It's first when we get to that point when the story piques my interest.<br /> <br /> I have nothing against Audrey Whitman and I don't want to offend anyone. But I didn't really feel the Chronicles of Darkness through this story. I think it would have been better if she cut down on the dialogue and tried to establish more mood, emotion and desperation. It was a pretty deadpan encounter with the supernatural.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>CREDITS AND SPECIAL THANKS</b><br /> <br /> I actually didn't know that Rose Bailey was the developer for the Chronicles of Darkness. I've lived with Onyx Path/White Wolf for a decade and I've been a member on the forums since back on the old forums in 2010. I confidently write and publish Exalted Homebrew. And I haven't even paid enough attention before to know that the Rose Bailey I see on the forums from time to time is the brains behind this operation. I really am clueless, aren't I? I actually feel kind of guilty for not having given the other OPP products more attention before now.<br /> <br /> I'm not very familiar with the other names, apart from Audrey's because I just read her intro fiction. I still don't know what the God Machine Chronicle is, but I see that there are some other writers working on that. It was originally written as a separate piece of content, wasn't it? Was the original intent to sell it separately or was it always meant to be part of this book? Don't tell me what it is yet. I'm thinking that it's an in game adventure of some kind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TABLE OF CONTENTS</b><br /> <br /> What I'm noticing here is that we seem to be jumping straight into character creation after the introduction. It doesn't have hundreds of pages of setting before we get into the actual character creation. My guess is that the idea here is that this book is a framework for the system and not a setting book. And if I want to apply these rules to create a game based in the \u201creal world\u201d, then why would I need to read a bunch of setting now? I'm okay with this.<br /> <br /> When looking over the table of contents, I notice a few terms I'm unfamiliar with: like<i>Anchors</i><b>.</b> Much of the rest is similar enough to Exalted to make me understand what they mean, but this one is new to me. Then we have <i>Aspirations</i> and <i>Breaking Points</i>. I assume that Aspirations are going to be tied to character motivations. No idea about Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> The <b>Dramatic Systems</b> mention some new stuff as well: <i>Conditions</i>, for example. I assume these are some kind of magical effect or something. The <i>Investigation</i> part of the rules seem heavy. Can't wait to get there. Then there's something called <i>Chases</i> that I have no idea what they are. I like that the combat part is called <i>Violence</i> instead of <i>Combat</i>.<br /> <br /> Oh, there's a <b>Storytelling</b> chapter. Nice.<br /> <br /> The <b>Antagonists</b> chapter seems to contain a lot of meat as well.<br /> <br /> Overall, my impressions are good and my interest is piqued. So this God Machine thing is half the book? That's interesting. Based on the table of contents, it looks like it has a lot of setting stuff. But I still don't know if it's a complete playable adventure, or if it's an alternative sandbox setting or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>SPREAD: \u201cWHERE THE SHADOWS GROW LONG\u201d</b><br /> <br /> Now this sets the mood for me. The book uses the cover art again but I find it much more effective here when there's an added context in the form of that quote. The blurry picture is growing on me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>INTRODUCTION</b></span><br /> <br /> I like the art and layout here. Mannequins will always be creepy.<br /> <br /> Now I finally got a description for what the God-Machine Chronicle is (I don't know if I'm supposed to write God-Machine or God Machine though since the book does both). So it is kind of what I suspected. I dunno what the God Machine actually is though. It reminds me of a fictional story I wrote way back, about a steam-noir setting where an ancient clockwork machine was located under a fascist 1940s style city where people could hear the cogs spinning in the ground below. Many worshiped the machine, but no one really knew what it was and where it came from.<br /> <br /> The <b>Inspirational Media</b> surprised me a little. The Crow and the Exorcist were given. The Terminator and True Detective surprised me. I expected more of a Friday the 13th and The Omen. Or maybe just a longer list. I do understand the reasoning though and I think it's a good idea to mention non-horror works as well as it could attract players who aren't normally horror fans (I'm not a horror fan, by the way---I'm a fan of suspense and good stories).<br /> <br /> I want all of the <b>Storytelling System Books</b>. I have Hurt Locker already and will be reading that one too when I'm done with this.<br /> <br /> Now the book lists all of the available splats. <i>Promethean</i> and <i>Geist</i> interest me. Not as something I want to buy right away, but as concepts I want to learn more about. My first splat will probably be <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> or <i>Hunter: The Vigil</i>. But we'll see.<br /> <br /> <b>LEXICON</b><br /> <br /> I'm not sure I understand what the system is getting at with the <i>Beat becomes Experience</i> system. Do I get Beats in a skill if I successfully use it, or do I get Beats in a pool for playing, that I then convert into XP that I then convert again into actual progression? Why not just use XP instead of a secondary thing? I guess I'll learn later.<br /> <br /> Ah, so <i>breaking point</i> is like a \u201csanity\u201d thing? The more a character is exposed to bad stuff, the more likely he is to be traumatized?<br /> <br /> The <i>chance roll </i>is interesting. I haven't seen that in other games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FICTION: \u201cTWO SIRAS\u201d</b><br /> <br /> Oooh. I enjoyed this. This was well-written and suspenseful. I wish it had been the intro fiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>THE FACE IN THE MIRROR: CHARACTERS</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>STEP ONE: CHARACTER CONCEPT</b><br /> <br /> It mentions <i>Aspirations </i>again and it's making me think of the Motivation system in Exalted 2nd Edition. It seems like you're supposed to have more than one Aspiration in this game though (based on the fact that it's mentioned in plural), so I assume it has some kind of important game mechanical application.<br /> <br /> <b>STEP TWO: ANCHORS</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so Anchors are tied to personality traits. I didn't see if there were an Intimacy system in this game so maybe Anchors and Aspirations are this game's variation to that. I'm curious to learn how they will work mechanically.<br /> <br /> <b>STEP SEVEN: DETERMINE ADVANTAGES</b><br /> <br /> I'm starting to realize now that this game works very different from what I'm used to in Exalted. There's something called Willpower in both games, and I have a feeling that this game's Willpower is different from that game's. I'm not going to try to assume that I know stuff now based on terminology.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">So Defense uses the lower of Wits or Dexterity for whatever Defense is used for. Since I'm picturing this as a dodge value of some kind, I'm surprised by the fact that it has two applicable Attributes. I don't really get why a trait that's probably important must ignore a stronger Attribute in favor of a weaker one. If both Attributes are important to the Defense value, why not use an average between the two traits? Or why not have two different Defense ratings based on different situations? I'm sure it'll clear up for me when I get to the system chapter.</span><br /> <br /> <b>ANCHORS</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">So the character's personality traits are anchored (pun intended) in the game system as a way for the character to spend/gain Willpower, but the characteristic cannot be something that's representative of an Attribute or Skill? When I determine these Anchors for my character, maybe I should focus on \u201chow\u201d she is and not \u201cwhat\u201d she is; avoid physical descriptions or synonyms for traits already represented and give attention to traits that represent <i>behavior</i>. Then me acting according to or against that behavior is what's helpful or detrimental to my Willpower. If I decide that my character has the Virtue \u201cplayful,\u201d I should be encouraged to roleplay in that way in order to regain Willpower? Is it also connected to <i>breaking points</i>? Am I understanding this correctly?</span><br /> <br /> So far I'm liking what I read. Giving the players incentives to act out their Anchors could do wonders to further roleplay.<br /> <br /> <b>ASPIRATIONS</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">This is an interesting idea that could encourage players to take more initiatives in game. But I'm <i>very </i>skeptical about the suggestion to have an Aspiration that encourages you to \u201cfail at something\u201d in order to make a better story. I don't really see how rewarding someone for failing at something should be encouraged. The act of roleplaying through both victories and defeat should feel rewarding. I don't need to write down an Aspiration to have fun. And I fear that it would make players meta-game their characters so that they fail at something for OOC reasons while their characters wouldn't try to fail at it IC. No, that seems like trouble to me.</span><br /> <br /> <b>BREAKING POINTS</b><br /> <br /> I like the idea of breaking points, but I didn't really understand here if there is a game system consequence for breaking or if the consequences of breaking is only in narrative. I guess it will be further explained later on.<br /> <br /> <b>ATTRIBUTES</b><br /> <br /> <i>Very </i>different form what I'm used to. I'm looking forward to learning more about how the actual system works.<br /> <br /> <b>SKILLS</b><br /> <br /> The fact that <i>Untrainted Skills </i>give -1 or -3 is something I'll probably forget about all the time.<br /> <br /> <b>MERITS</b><br /> <br /> I enjoy the large number of Merits. I may even steal some of them and homebrew them into Exalted Third Edition. I'm not familiar with the mechanics yet to comment on individual Merits. I didn't actually expect that Merits would cover so many supernatural abilities, such as <i>Telekinesis</i> and <i>Telepathy</i>. They seem to be the true meat of character customization so far.<br /> <br /> <br /> My impressions of the game now after having read up to this point is that it seems like a fairly simple system but that can hold substantial depth. The Merit system lets you customize pretty much any character concept, with potential for homebrewing more Merits. The layout is rather simple, but clean and effective. I do miss colors though, and the blue hue is kind of boring and tiring. There are many different visual styles in the art pieces scattered across the pages. I can't say I like all of them, but almost all of them fit well enough into the layout. I tolerate the odd ones out here more than some of the awkward Poser pieces in Exalted Third Edition.<br /> <br /> I'm going to leave it at this for now and continue with <b>Infernal Systems: Dramatic Engine</b> at another time in another post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit: Since this is a thread of me talking to myself, it's not really clear when I'm rhethorical and when I seriously want to a discussion about it. I'm going to do this: <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Blue text means that I'd like to discuss this further</span>. <span style=\"color:#008000\">Green text means that I'm interested in further discussion but that I think that I already know the answer or that I'll soon figure it out.</span> Then I can just add the color when I'm done writing the post without needing to go back to edit any of my initial impressions.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 02-18-2017, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T14:31:32-08:00","id":1051147,"title":"","content":"Readthroughs in this format are always a fascinating and valuable exercise. Since following your thought process as the book presents information to you is critical, I want to ask: <b>are there any particular questions or wonderings in your writing so far that you <i>would</i> like direct responses to?</b> For instance, is &quot;am I understanding this correctly?&quot; under Anchors rhetorical, or a query to the forums?<br /> <br /> I do think it's safe to specify: the Vampire game you played a decade ago was <i>probably</i> Vampire: the Masquerade, not Vampire: the Requiem. Masquerade, Reckoning, and Ascension are part of an older set of gamelines, now (since intellectual property changed hands, business stuff) officially titled the World of Darkness; as you've already read, the set of gamelines now called the Chronicles of Darkness is different, differentiated by subtitles where appropriate. It's definitely understandable if that bit is confusing. The mechanical heritage of White Wolf games kind of started with the original World of Darkness system, and then branched in different directions, with Exalted's system being one direction, and the Chronicles system being another. So you will see significant similarities alongside significant divergences, as again, I think you probably have noticed already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T14:59:21-08:00","id":1051162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051147#post1051147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Readthroughs in this format are always a fascinating and valuable exercise. Since following your thought process as the book presents information to you is critical, I want to ask: <b>are there any particular questions or wonderings in your writing so far that you <i>would</i> like direct responses to?</b> For instance, is &quot;am I understanding this correctly?&quot; under Anchors rhetorical, or a query to the forums?<br /> <br /> I do think it's safe to specify: the Vampire game you played a decade ago was <i>probably</i> Vampire: the Masquerade, not Vampire: the Requiem. Masquerade, Reckoning, and Ascension are part of an older set of gamelines, now (since intellectual property changed hands, business stuff) officially titled the World of Darkness; as you've already read, the set of gamelines now called the Chronicles of Darkness is different, differentiated by subtitles where appropriate. It's definitely understandable if that bit is confusing. The mechanical heritage of White Wolf games kind of started with the original World of Darkness system, and then branched in different directions, with Exalted's system being one direction, and the Chronicles system being another. So you will see significant similarities alongside significant divergences, as again, I think you probably have noticed already.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant to write &quot;the Masquerade&quot;. Writing &quot;the Requiem&quot; was a typo.<br /> <br /> It's true that some questions I pose are rethorical since I often answer my own questions as I keep reading, and I don't really want to go back and edit stuff retroactively because I want to retain my initial impressions. For this post, I would like to hear people's thoughts about my questions under &quot;Aspirations&quot; in particular. I'm also curious about my Defense thoughts, but that's something I may figure out when I delve into the next chapter too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:06:06-08:00","id":1051167,"title":"","content":"This is awesome and I can't wait to hear more of your impressions of the book! I'll second Looseman's query if you want actual answers to some of your questions or if you are just posing them rhetorically and want to wait and see what the book has to say. If you do I'd be happy to answer.<br /> <br /> It's also really, <i>really</i> hard to refrain from talking about the God-Machine Chronicle and what it is, but I'll hold my tongue since it's clear you want to sort out what you can on your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:19:26-08:00","id":1051173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051167#post1051167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is awesome and I can't wait to hear more of your impressions of the book! I'll second Looseman's query if you want actual answers to some of your questions or if you are just posing them rhetorically and want to wait and see what the book has to say. If you do I'd be happy to answer.<br /> <br /> It's also really, <i>really</i> hard to refrain from talking about the God-Machine Chronicle and what it is, but I'll hold my tongue since it's clear you want to sort out what you can on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I edited my original post in a way that will let people know what I'm genuinely interested in discussing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:25:14-08:00","id":1051177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051173#post1051173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I edited my original post in a way that will let people know what I'm genuinely interested in discussing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh. Could you please edit it again and change that red to another color? Red text is generally used by the mods to indicate official communication, so we prefer other members not use it to avoid confusion. Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:28:28-08:00","id":1051181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051177#post1051177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh. Could you please edit it again and change that red to another color? Red text is generally used by the mods to indicate official communication, so we prefer other members not use it to avoid confusion. Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div>There we go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T16:00:31-08:00","id":1051196,"title":"","content":"Note on aspirations: It's less on &quot;succeeding/failing at a roll&quot; and more &quot;succeeding/failing at a endeavor&quot;. I've personally never taken a &quot;negative&quot; aspiration, but I can see how it'd work in say, Vampire or Werewolf. An aspiration such as &quot;drive my loved ones away from what I've become&quot; could be phrased in different ways. Interesting takes could be &quot;Failing at keeping the Beast/Rage/Obsessions at bay.&quot;<br /> <br /> All of those generate plenty of dramatic tension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T16:02:14-08:00","id":1051197,"title":"","content":"@ Anchors, yeah seems you understand them.<br /> @ Aspirations, so far aspirations which are &quot;Fail at x thing&quot; or &quot;X bad thing happens&quot; haven't caused any metagaming issues, but of course every group is different, and even some people in my group were like &quot;Wait, why would we want aspirations which screwed ourselves over?&quot; at first. It's important to remember that the aspirations are more an attribute tied to the player than it is tied to the character. But care should be taken if one of your players does think up an interesting &quot;fail aspiration&quot; that the other players are fine with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T16:29:12-08:00","id":1051207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing#post1051116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">So Defense uses the lower of Wits or Dexterity for whatever Defense is used for. Since I'm picturing this as a dodge value of some kind, I'm surprised by the fact that it has two applicable Attributes. I don't really get why a trait that's probably important must ignore a stronger Attribute in favor of a weaker one. If both Attributes are important to the Defense value, why not use an average between the two traits? Or why not have two different Defense ratings based on different situations? I'm sure it'll clear up for me when I get to the system chapter.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is partially a verisimilitude thing - being agile doesn't help you avoid getting hit if you're not quick-thinking enough to react to the incoming attack in time, and having fast reflexes doesn't help if you're too clumsy to act on them effectively. As for the specific execution of that idea (lower of the two traits instead of average or some other calculation), that will probably become more clear when you get to the violence section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing#post1051116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">So the character's personality traits are anchored (pun intended) in the game system as a way for the character to spend/gain Willpower, but the characteristic cannot be something that's representative of an Attribute or Skill? When I determine these Anchors for my character, maybe I should focus on \u201chow\u201d she is and not \u201cwhat\u201d she is; avoid physical descriptions or synonyms for traits already represented and give attention to traits that represent <i>behavior</i>. Then me acting according to or against that behavior is what's helpful or detrimental to my Willpower. If I decide that my character has the Virtue \u201cplayful,\u201d I should be encouraged to roleplay in that way in order to regain Willpower? Is it also connected to <i>breaking points</i>? Am I understanding this correctly?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>You are understanding correctly, yes. And anchors do play a small role in Breaking Points, and in the Social Maneuvering subsystem, but their primary purpose is to guide roleplaying and to provide a means of recovering spent Willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing#post1051116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">This is an interesting idea that could encourage players to take more initiatives in game. But I'm <i>very </i>skeptical about the suggestion to have an Aspiration that encourages you to \u201cfail at something\u201d in order to make a better story. I don't really see how rewarding someone for failing at something should be encouraged. The act of roleplaying through both victories and defeat should feel rewarding. I don't need to write down an Aspiration to have fun. And I fear that it would make players meta-game their characters so that they fail at something for OOC reasons while their characters wouldn't try to fail at it IC. No, that seems like trouble to me.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>So, if this rubs you the wrong way, there are a few other things in the system that I think may give you similar vibes. This is part of a general design philosophy for 2e where roleplaying behavior should be encouraged, not forced, and should be encouraged with carrots, not with sticks. That said, I wouldn't worry too much about it causing meta-gaming. A big part of the purpose of Aspirations is to give the players an in-system way to communicate to the storyteller what direction they would like to see the story go. Taking an aspiration to fail at something is a little like including loose ends in a character backstory in that sense. It sends a signal saying &quot;This is an avenue of character development I would like to explore, and you are welcome to use this as a means of introducing drama into the game.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T16:55:11-08:00","id":1051220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051207#post1051207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It sends a signal saying &quot;This is an avenue of character development I would like to explore, and you are welcome to use this as a means of introducing drama into the game.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>One good example I've seen is an aspiration which said they wanted to save their family, meaning I as storyteller would be allowed to go for their family to make drama without having to worry about players feeling like &quot;if you have a character in your backstory they will be targeted meaning I should be a loner orphan in future games&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:10:29-08:00","id":1051227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#008000\">So Defense uses the lower of Wits or Dexterity for whatever Defense is used for. Since I'm picturing this as a dodge value of some kind, I'm surprised by the fact that it has two applicable Attributes. I don't really get why a trait that's probably important must ignore a stronger Attribute in favor of a weaker one. If both Attributes are important to the Defense value, why not use an average between the two traits? Or why not have two different Defense ratings based on different situations? I'm sure it'll clear up for me when I get to the system chapter.</span> </div> </div> </div>I would say it's primarily due to the small scale on which Attributes are typically rated, and the slow rate at which they're increased in play. An average would be unwieldy because the difference between Wits and Dexterity is very frequently a single dot, having just one Defense trait keeps things simpler and moving smoother (combat doesn't generally go for the kind of mechanical detail Exalted does), ticking the average Defense value down a point contributes to the system generally favoring dynamic violence by privileging offense, and it opens up a little design space in that there are certain situations where characters do use the higher of the two Attributes, usually as the result of a particular power or Merit, or as a general perk making wild animals a bit more dangerous physically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>ANCHORS</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">So the character's personality traits are anchored (pun intended) in the game system as a way for the character to spend/gain Willpower, but the characteristic cannot be something that's representative of an Attribute or Skill? When I determine these Anchors for my character, maybe I should focus on \u201chow\u201d she is and not \u201cwhat\u201d she is; avoid physical descriptions or synonyms for traits already represented and give attention to traits that represent <i>behavior</i>. Then me acting according to or against that behavior is what's helpful or detrimental to my Willpower. If I decide that my character has the Virtue \u201cplayful,\u201d I should be encouraged to roleplay in that way in order to regain Willpower? Is it also connected to <i>breaking points</i>? Am I understanding this correctly?</span> </div> </div> </div>You're pretty much on exactly the right track. Virtue and Vice function the best when they are about what stakes you are fighting for (Virtue) or what quirks and behavioral tics you lean on (Vice), rather than being too particular or process-based. Generally, Virtue is a higher drive that comes into play in situations where you are risking everything or going to extremes: you become able to exert heroic effort in favor of your Virtue without totally exhausting yourself. Vice is a weakness or tic that is very frequently tempting to feed in lesser ways, and comes into play during slower or safer times, as an easy comfort to keep you going.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>ASPIRATIONS</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">This is an interesting idea that could encourage players to take more initiatives in game. But I'm <i>very </i>skeptical about the suggestion to have an Aspiration that encourages you to \u201cfail at something\u201d in order to make a better story. I don't really see how rewarding someone for failing at something should be encouraged. The act of roleplaying through both victories and defeat should feel rewarding. I don't need to write down an Aspiration to have fun. And I fear that it would make players meta-game their characters so that they fail at something for OOC reasons while their characters wouldn't try to fail at it IC. No, that seems like trouble to me.</span> </div> </div> </div>The Chronicles of Darkness second edition system you're reading is going to need a little buy-in to what it's trying to do, and you'll find that to get into its playspace properly, you're going to have to warm up to the idea of player decisions not always directly lining up with the player character's best interests. CofD is a system that wants characters to strive, but not always for things they should strive for; it has systems you've not read yet that exist to reinforce and incentivize behavior that is genre-appropriate for a horror game where people make mistakes that get them into trouble or contribute to their undoing.<br /> <br /> Aspirations often function best as a convenient flag to the Storyteller to indicate plot beats you're interested in exploring as a player, and not all of the story situations we enjoy when consuming media are positive for the character in-universe. You might think of Dale Cooper's sheet containing the aspiration &quot;encounter an uncanny similarity or omen,&quot; or Luke Skywalker's sheet saying &quot;discover a fateful secret about my father.&quot; They're not always things the character is personally working to bring about, but they're parts of these characters stories, and often some of the most memorable and entertaining ones. Story feeds off conflict, and one function of Aspirations is to help the Storyteller align their idea of what conflicts are interesting and fun with their players'.<br /> <br /> Truth be told, despite putting this argument forth, I'm not the biggest fan of the aspiration subsystem for different reasons: I find it fiddly in play, slowing things down to keep thinking of aspirations in ways that outweigh the benefit of an explicit dialogue on what everybody wants to see in the game. And there <i>is</i> an occasional, though rare, mechanic that does treat a character's aspirations as a more internal description of what the player character is actively seeking out, so my view of it is not completely consonant with the rules as written. I can say that it's super easy work to house rule them out and just add a couple beats a session to replace their role in progression. They're not a central part of the CofD system.<br /> <br /> But another thing, later, is, and it will confront you with a similar divide between player intent and character intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:52:09-08:00","id":1051247,"title":"","content":"Defence is deducted from the dice pool for the attack, most of the time it doesn't apply to being shot at because bullets move fast. Other than that you seem to be on track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T00:51:28-08:00","id":1051406,"title":"","content":"Aspirations seem like a headache to be honest. It's too soon to tell this early into the read, but I have a feeling I'll put some restriction on aspirations to only represent the character's goals and not the player's. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051247#post1051247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defence is deducted from the dice pool for the attack, most of the time it doesn't apply to being shot at because bullets move fast. Other than that you seem to be on track.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? So in theory, there are enemies who are so good at defending that you're practically incapable of attacking them (if their Defense is higher than your attack pool)? I guess this is where the chance roll comes into play to give you at least a small chance of hitting a big bad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T01:06:00-08:00","id":1051410,"title":"","content":"Yep, some of the supernaturals can get it absurdly high. You can dodge instead of using your defence which lets you roll double your defence and deduct the successes from your opponents successes but doing so uses your action for the turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T01:38:36-08:00","id":1051423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051406#post1051406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspirations seem like a headache to be honest. It's too soon to tell this early into the read, but I have a feeling I'll put some restriction on aspirations to only represent the character's goals and not the player's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Example Aspirations are good thing to point out to characters. For<b> Mage the Awakening</b> I made list of Obsessions ( special Aspirations for mages, like general mystical and magical researches they take ) based on characters Orders - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040062-2e-guide-how-to-choose-your-obsessions?p=1041061#post1041061\">here is list</a>.<br /> <br /> My general advice for <b>CoD</b> games is simple - <b>Read players characters concepts and as ST suggest what Aspirations they can take</b> - think general motivations of characters. <b>ALSO let them declare Aspirations in middle of game sessions, if they have free slots.</b> By the time of second or third game sessions, if you remind them on start of game to choose Aspirations, they will take themselves all that is need and will gorge in this for all the Beats they want. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051406#post1051406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? So in theory, there are enemies who are so good at defending that you're practically incapable of attacking them (if their Defense is higher than your attack pool)? I guess this is where the chance roll comes into play to give you at least a small chance of hitting a big bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>And Willpower points that gives almost always character +3 to any dicepool. <b>This is why you need Willpower point pool in the first place</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-19-2017, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T03:01:59-08:00","id":1051442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051406#post1051406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspirations seem like a headache to be honest. It's too soon to tell this early into the read, but I have a feeling I'll put some restriction on aspirations to only represent the character's goals and not the player's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aspirations really aren't that bad, even with &quot;negative&quot; ones.<br /> <br /> One of the big things about anything that gives Beats in the game, is that Beats mostly come from plot important things: successes and failures, ups and downs.<br /> <br /> This is because the CofD is a horror setting at its core. Bad stuff is supposed to happen to the characters. Things like negative Aspirations are just a way to make the bad stuff as much a part of the game rewards as the good stuff, to reward players for engaging in the genre over just thinking about what's the best thing from their character's perspective.<br /> <br /> It might help to think of it like taking a high dot value Virtue in Exalted 1e/2e: that's a double edged sword that can aid your character or hold your character back. Aspirations are just a more fluid and flexible idea a long the same lines. Taking a high Temperance character in Exalted isn't just saying, &quot;my character is awesome at resisting temptation,&quot; but also saying, &quot;my character has trouble bending the rules or indulging in pleasures.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really? So in theory, there are enemies who are so good at defending that you're practically incapable of attacking them (if their Defense is higher than your attack pool)? I guess this is where the chance roll comes into play to give you at least a small chance of hitting a big bad? </div> </div> </div>As noted this is correct. Though in general attacks vs. standard defense are going to have a slight edge. For the investment it's easier to keep attack pools 1-3 dice higher than defense pools, though a tough fight can easily put you into a chance die (since there are other penalties out their besides the target's defense on top of facing someone that's built for defense), but there's a lot later in the book that provides options for trying to shove it back in the attacker's favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T08:10:18-08:00","id":1051524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051406#post1051406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspirations seem like a headache to be honest. It's too soon to tell this early into the read, but I have a feeling I'll put some restriction on aspirations to only represent the character's goals and not the player's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't bother with Aspirations at all a lot of the time. I run one-offs and short-run games more often than extended campaigns, so Aspirations don't really work for me a lot of the time. They're very easy to remove if you don't like them, just give the players a few extra Beats to compensate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051406#post1051406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? So in theory, there are enemies who are so good at defending that you're practically incapable of attacking them (if their Defense is higher than your attack pool)? I guess this is where the chance roll comes into play to give you at least a small chance of hitting a big bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without getting too much into the specific details of the violence system before you'be had a chance to read it, yes. The math slightly favors attack pools over Defense (this is one of the reasons Defense keys off of the lower of two values), but it is entirely possible for someone who specializes in Defense to reduce an unspecialized attacker's pool to a chance die. There are ways to boost your dice pools though, such as spending Willpower and making all-out attacks. Also, fights in CofD tend to be short and brutal. Not for nothing is it named violence rather than combat. One good hit is often all it takes to end a fight, unless the opponent is just in it for violence's sake (which some monsters are, to be fair).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T12:04:29-08:00","id":1051601,"title":"","content":"Very cool that you are doing a readthrough. I look forward to seeing what you have to say. One note, if Promethean peaks your interest, I would strongly suggest giving Promethean 2e the readthrough treatment. Promethean was the gateway through which I discovered the rest of the Chronicles of Darkness (then the New World of Darkness), and it is absolutely enthralling. 2e took a great game and made it even better. I just got by own premium print of it last week, and it is gorgeous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T12:25:22-08:00","id":1051612,"title":"","content":"Let's keep going.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FICTION: \u201cHUNGRY WOLF\u201d</b><br /> <br /> Hmm. I liked how this story ended. It was a bit short and tame otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>INFERNAL ENGINES: DRAMATIC SYSTEMS</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ROLLING DICE</b><br /> <br /> This explains how to make dice pools which I'm familiar with. But as an Exalted player, I dread the idea that 7s aren't successes anymore. I don't think it's bad to have 8s or above, but I do think it's a bit scary. I'm also not used to the fact that you reroll all 10s instead of counting them as two successes. But overall, it's simple.<br /> <br /> So there is no dice difficulty apart from the bonuses or penalties? Instead of saying that \u201cyou need three successes to succeed\u201d, you always only need one success but difficulties add modifiers? And if you by some chance roll five successes, you get a beneficial <i>Condition</i> (which is something I'll learn about later). Seems straightforward.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Does equipment modifiers stack or do you use the highest modifier? If my suit gives me +1 to Presence or whatever, but my cool haircut also gives +1 to Presence, do I still have +1 to Presence or do I have +2? If I can stack modifiers, are they capped at +3 unless there's an \u201cextreme situation\u201d? What if there are several extreme situations? The house is burning AND the ceiling is caving in AND I have a rash. Am I still at -5? Can my cool haircut reduce the penalty to -4 instead? Though I assume the coolest haircuts are quite flammable, so perhaps I should have another penalty for that.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ATTRIBUTE TASKS</b><br /> <br /> You can roll an Attribute with another Attribute? That just blew my mind.<br /> <br /> It will probably take some time for me to get a feel for which Attribute + Attribute or Attribute + Skill combination suits specific actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ACTIONS</b><br /> <br /> So there is no mention of threshold successes when describing contested actions. It says that the victor needs to roll more successes. I assume that an equal number of successes is a failure then?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EXTENDED ACTIONS</b><br /> <br /> So extended actions are the only types of action (apart from contested ones) that may require more than a single success to be successful?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>RESISTANCE</b><br /> <br /> This is the first time where I learn about a type of action where the number of successes mean something; namely for violence. So the enemy's Resistance trait is their Defense which reduces a number of dice from my attack, and the number of my successes then affect the damage of said attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>PERMUTATIONS</b><br /> <br /> Some weapons add successes (supposedly to the aforementioned attack roll). So the combat system bypasses the whole \u201cdamage rolling part\u201d from Exalted and does acurracy and damage as a single roll? <i>Rote Actions</i> seem a bit generous. I can picture some situations where they can be used though. If my \u201cdoctor character\u201d diagnoses a wound that's easy and normally wouldn't require a roll, the fact that she's under heavy fire could be the cause of a Rote Action where her knowledge as a doctor justifies the action being easy, but the current circumstances are such that the ST wants a chance for failure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TIME</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Does anyone actually use the term \u201cChapter\u201d to describe a story outside of the text in this book? Or do you just say \u201csession\u201d. I'm curious. I understand that they want a theme in the book, but everyone is going to say \u201clet's play a session of CofD\u201d and not \u201clet's play a chapter of CofD.\u201d It's pretty language, but I doubt even Rose Bailey uses that term. If she does, I apologize \u2026 but she should just say \u201csession.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> I know I'm nitpicky.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>WILLPOWER</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Does spending Willpower to gain a bonus stack with other modifiers that give bonuses? Remember that cool haircut I mentioned? Either way it's a powerful tool. And based on what I'm reading here, it seems fairly easy to just replenish it through your Anchors at the scene's end.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>BREAKING POINT</b><br /> <br /> This part of the book is copy-pasted from the Character Creation chapter. It's a pretty big part to just copy and paste. Finally there is some info about how it works in practice though. I can see some problems I'm going to have with one particular player of mine when it comes to breaking points. I know that I'm going to want to be generous with them, because I want to represent human nature. One of my players has a big ego and always have problems with characters that display weakness. We're going to have lots of arguments over what constitutes his Mary Sues' breaking points. Such is the life of an ST, I guess.<br /> <br /> The more I read about <i>Conditions</i>, the more silly I feel for being convinced they were just \u201cmagical effects\u201d when I read the table of contents.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>CONDITIONS</b><br /> <br /> Here we go. Just wait for a moment.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm back.</b> Just went over to DrivethruRPG to buy the physical <i>Condition Cards</i>. Also got the <i>Tilt Cards</i> while I was there. Apparently shipping to Sweden is 27 dollars. Oh well. It'll probably be twice that when the walls are up.<br /> <br /> Without actually having read what any of the Conditions do yet, I get the feeling that they could really shake up the dynamic in game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EXPERIENCE</b><br /> <br /> Finally a description about Beats and how they work. I'm not really sure why we need to call these mini-XP Beats when we can just call them XP and then increase the costs of everything by five. If I fulfill an Aspiration to earn a Beat, why should I wait until after the game session (Hah! The book didn't call it Chapter! I knew it was silly) instead of replacing the aspiration immediately or during the session?<br /> <br /> So if we removed Beats, renamed them XP (sorry, <i>Experiences</i>), then the chart would look like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute:</b> 20 Experiences per dot.<br /> <b>Merits:</b> 5 Experiences per dot.<br /> <b>Skill Specialty:</b> 5 Experiences per dot.<br /> <b>Skill:</b> 10 Experiences per dot.<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 10 Experiences per dot.<br /> <br /> It does the exact same thing as converting Beats into XP, and it feels like the only reason to have Beats in the game is to keep the Experience numbers low. It's a bit of a pet peeve of mine to go around calling something what it is just to add a tad of assumed originality to a product. It's XP (experience points). Not Beats. And not Experiences. Call it what it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>INVESTIGATION</b><br /> <br /> Under <b>No Hard Answers</b>, it mentions that you should let your players come up with their own clues. I've never liked that as a player and I've never liked that as a storyteller. I have no problems with some creative freedoms when it comes to the setting around the characters, but I've never liked that \u201cshared storytelling\u201d concept. I want the storyteller to be one thing and the player to be one thing, and I don't like mixing the two. That's why I couldn't get into the <a href=\"https://swallowsofthesouth.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Swallows of the South</i></a> podcast.<br /> <br /> I was going to make a comment about how the Investigations part feels like it should be in the Storytelling chapter but then it told me that a clue is a type of equipment. Now I'm all \u201cwhat does that mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> And I'm not convinced. It seems like a big part of the game, but it also seems like an immersion-breaking mini game. Can't I just solve everything through narration with the occasional bonuses/penalties to actions instead of having to count elements and go \u201cNo you can't benefit from that clue anymore because you're out of elements so sucky for you that the librarian doesn't believe you and will refuse to lead you to the secret parts of the library where the next clue is. You shouldn't have used up your elements on the police guy!\u201d<br /> <br /> Yeah, this clue thing is making me lose interest fast in the Investigations aspect of this game.<br /> <br /> \u201cOnce characters reach the required number of Clues, they're able to Uncover the Truth if that's their goal. They can do so without any additional rolls if they spend a number of Clue elements (divided however they like) equal to the required Clues for the investigation.\u201d WHAT DOES THAT EVEN MEAN?<br /> <br /> Why can't it just be \u201cPresent a fun and suspenseful story to your players. Let them uncover a number of clues that could, if used correctly, lead them to uncover the mystery. Use the clues as elements to further enhance the story, but also present new challenges to the players as they uncover these clues.\u201d See. All you need to do is roleplay.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh wait, we're playing Chronicles of Darkness. Go get your calculators, folks! Let's start up the Excel sheet! These clue elements won't divide themselves!\u201d<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">As you can tell, I'm not a fan of this whole clue element mini game. It feels very much like something from a board game without substantial content. I've always roleplayed investigation scenarios by letting players find actual narrated clues without any specific properties. The clues have always been what the players made of them, and the players themselves had to recognize the value of the clues as well as what to do with them. I want to present a story, where every clue is a part of that story. Please tell me that this part is optional because I can't see myself being sold on it.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> And with that, I'm going to call it for today and start with the Social Manuevering part another time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T12:58:18-08:00","id":1051623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Does equipment modifiers stack or do you use the highest modifier? If my suit gives me +1 to Presence or whatever, but my cool haircut also gives +1 to Presence, do I still have +1 to Presence or do I have +2? If I can stack modifiers, are they capped at +3 unless there's an \u201cextreme situation\u201d? What if there are several extreme situations? The house is burning AND the ceiling is caving in AND I have a rash. Am I still at -5? Can my cool haircut reduce the penalty to -4 instead? Though I assume the coolest haircuts are quite flammable, so perhaps I should have another penalty for that.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Bonuses do stack, but are capped at -5 <i>after applying penalties</i>, and likewise penalties stack but are capped at -5 after applying bonuses. So, if you've got a total of +9 from various bonuses and a total of -3 from various penalties, you and up with a total bonus of +6 after penalties, which is over the +5 cap, so you get +5 bonus on the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Does anyone actually use the term \u201cChapter\u201d to describe a story outside of the text in this book? Or do you just say \u201csession\u201d. I'm curious. I understand that they want a theme in the book, but everyone is going to say \u201clet's play a session of CofD\u201d and not \u201clet's play a chapter of CofD.\u201d It's pretty language, but I doubt even Rose Bailey uses that term. If she does, I apologize \u2026 but she should just say \u201csession.\u201d</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of like calling the GM a storyteller, or the adventure a story. Some people always do it. Some people never do it. Most people use both interchangably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Does spending Willpower to gain a bonus stack with other modifiers that give bonuses? Remember that cool haircut I mentioned? Either way it's a powerful tool. And based on what I'm reading here, it seems fairly easy to just replenish it through your Anchors at the scene's end.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually not 100% sure what the RAW answer is on this. I <i>think</i> the bonus from Willpower can apply on top of the +(up to 5) from equipment. That's how I run it, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally a description about Beats and how they work. I'm not really sure why we need to call these mini-XP Beats when we can just call them XP and then increase the costs of everything by five. If I fulfill an Aspiration to earn a Beat, why should I wait until after the game session (Hah! The book didn't call it Chapter! I knew it was silly) instead of replacing the aspiration immediately or during the session?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you didn't put this part in blue or green, but it seemed important to address. First of all, yeah, you can totally just call Beats exp and multiply the costs by 5 if you want to. You wouldn't be the first. As for why you should wait until after the session to replace fulfilled Aspirations, I can answer that from experience (hah!). My first CofD campaign, I ruled that players could replace Aspirations as soon as they had been fulfilled. Aspirations very quickly stopped being about the players sending me signals about where they wanted to see the game go, and started being about the players trying to guess what would happen next that session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">As you can tell, I'm not a fan of this whole clue element mini game. It feels very much like something from a board game without substantial content. I've always roleplayed investigation scenarios by letting players find actual narrated clues without any specific properties. The clues have always been what the players made of them, and the players themselves had to recognize the value of the clues as well as what to do with them. I want to present a story, where every clue is a part of that story. Please tell me that this part is optional because I can't see myself being sold on it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It is purely optional and you are not alone in disliking it. I refused to touch the Investigations system for a long time for similar reasons, though I've come up with a heavily hacked version that I am mostly satisfied with. But don't worry about it, there are only a handful of Merits that interact with the Investigation system, and it's easy to just tell your players &quot;don't take any Merits that mention Clues, they're part of an optional subsystem I'm not using.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-19-2017, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T13:06:11-08:00","id":1051627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051623#post1051623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspirations very quickly stopped being about the players sending me signals about where they wanted to see the game go, and started being about the players trying to guess what would happen next that session.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see how that could be a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T13:08:26-08:00","id":1051629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Does equipment modifiers stack or do you use the highest modifier? If my suit gives me +1 to Presence or whatever, but my cool haircut also gives +1 to Presence, do I still have +1 to Presence or do I have +2? If I can stack modifiers, are they capped at +3 unless there's an \u201cextreme situation\u201d? What if there are several extreme situations? The house is burning AND the ceiling is caving in AND I have a rash. Am I still at -5? Can my cool haircut reduce the penalty to -4 instead? Though I assume the coolest haircuts are quite flammable, so perhaps I should have another penalty for that.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>You can get ANYTHING up to +/- 5 in the sum up to starting dicepool. But ST judgment is advised.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>ATTRIBUTE TASKS</b><br /> <br /> You can roll an Attribute with another Attribute? That just blew my mind.<br /> <br /> It will probably take some time for me to get a feel for which Attribute + Attribute or Attribute + Skill combination suits specific actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typical Attrubute rolls are Perception or 'Do I see...' roll ( Wits + Composure ) and 'Mental Resistance' ( Resolve + Composure ). There are others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>ACTIONS</b><br /> <br /> So there is no mention of threshold successes when describing contested actions. It says that the victor needs to roll more successes. I assume that an equal number of successes is a failure then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Equal number is a <i>tie</i>. Like you did not won, but your enemy also. On Olympics you may both get Gold Medal, as both went to the needed threshold. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>EXTENDED ACTIONS</b><br /> <br /> So extended actions are the only types of action (apart from contested ones) that may require more than a single success to be successful?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Chases, Invesitgations and Social Manuvering, but they are basiclly permutations on Extended Actions sub-system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>TIME</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Does anyone actually use the term \u201cChapter\u201d to describe a story outside of the text in this book? Or do you just say \u201csession\u201d. I'm curious. I understand that they want a theme in the book, but everyone is going to say \u201clet's play a session of CofD\u201d and not \u201clet's play a chapter of CofD.\u201d It's pretty language, but I doubt even Rose Bailey uses that term. If she does, I apologize \u2026 but she should just say \u201csession.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> I know I'm nitpicky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Session is all forum used. Chapter is much more books term.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>WILLPOWER</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Does spending Willpower to gain a bonus stack with other modifiers that give bonuses? Remember that cool haircut I mentioned? Either way it's a powerful tool. And based on what I'm reading here, it seems fairly easy to just replenish it through your Anchors at the scene's end.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time, you can simply burn Willpower to rise your dicepool. I even let to run with it from +5 to +8 on the roll.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying Anchors is <i>good</i>, we always encourage to play on the Anchors. Most of the time playing on the is not that easy - Virtue one need to make something at stake and you can only use it twice per chapter/session. Vice leads to it's own complications....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>BREAKING POINT</b><br /> <br /> This part of the book is copy-pasted from the Character Creation chapter. It's a pretty big part to just copy and paste. Finally there is some info about how it works in practice though. I can see some problems I'm going to have with one particular player of mine when it comes to breaking points. I know that I'm going to want to be generous with them, because I want to represent human nature. One of my players has a big ego and always have problems with characters that display weakness. We're going to have lots of arguments over what constitutes his Mary Sues' breaking points. Such is the life of an ST, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I run Breaking Points as 'biggest penalty I give and players are lawyering to lower it' - so one character has kidnapped NPC. I treated it as making more or less the same impact as Torture - so PC on start may roll with -3 penalty. Then player argue 'but I'm doing this with my Virtue' - and get's +1, so now roll is on -2. Then he says 'but our traditions says we should do this' or 'king approved my course of action' and get's next +1, ending with only -1 to roll. Of course, there is needed to be put boundary on to how character can easy Breaking Point, but in the end, he will <b>still</b> roll it and still get at least one Beat of it. Players <i>should be encouraged</i> to try Breaking Points - more they roll but have good results, the more chance someday they will not pass the roll... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />( And for each Breaking Point roll, they still get Beat, and maybe second from resolving Condition from it. )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>INVESTIGATION</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">As you can tell, I'm not a fan of this whole clue element mini game. It feels very much like something from a board game without substantial content. I've always roleplayed investigation scenarios by letting players find actual narrated clues without any specific properties. The clues have always been what the players made of them, and the players themselves had to recognize the value of the clues as well as what to do with them. I want to present a story, where every clue is a part of that story. Please tell me that this part is optional because I can't see myself being sold on it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Investigations subsystem ( just like Chase, Horrors and Social Maneuvering ) are OPTIONAL to use. ( Well, Social Maneuvering is everywhere in 2E books and connected to some secondary mechanics of characters, but still assumed to be used as option rather than forced. )<br /> <br /> Investigation system works <i>great</i> if you got some Mystery plot in mind and <b>want's</b> characters to collect little evidence. Then just each Clue, really, is small part of greater puzzle. And Elements are bonuses character <b>can</b> use as Equipment to actions related to case, not <i>must</i> use in Investigation. You need general number of Clues collected, but can end with even ZERO Elements - just ending will be much more 'bloody' for characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Myself, I used is as basis for 'extensive reaserchs' ( where PCs spends days in libraries or weird occult sources to know Ban &amp; Bane of particular Ephemeral Entity or Horror, for example ) and also not use 'players make up Clue' - it's really to much indy rpg to my taste. What I let character is to LOOK for the Clues in specific way and then I describe it -'You look in to County records? Great, roll Wits+Politics, pay 50$ bribe to working clerk and you find... the last property documents on your suspect. It get's you as one Clue with 2 Elements.' Things like that. I advise to look over in detail<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues\"> this topic solely on Investigations subsystem</a> and try to use <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/804287-cofd-clue-cards-for-investigations\">Clues Cards</a> I invented and <b>Mr Gone</b> done for us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-19-2017, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T09:54:51-08:00","id":1052039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but I've never liked that \u201cshared storytelling\u201d concept. I want the storyteller to be one thing and the player to be one thing, and I don't like mixing the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is going to come up more. Like with Aspirations, a lot of CofD 2e uses the idea that the players and the Storyteller are gathering to tell a story together. Not just that the players are there to react to the GM's story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">As you can tell, I'm not a fan of this whole clue element mini game. It feels very much like something from a board game without substantial content. I've always roleplayed investigation scenarios by letting players find actual narrated clues without any specific properties. The clues have always been what the players made of them, and the players themselves had to recognize the value of the clues as well as what to do with them. I want to present a story, where every clue is a part of that story. Please tell me that this part is optional because I can't see myself being sold on it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I have some advice here, and it is going to come in handy for the next section on Social Manuevering. Don't think of them as mini-games, don't stop and 'do an Investiagtion'. The Clues are the same as the narrative clues you had before, only this gives you a system to track how many clues the players have gathered and a system that doesn't just rely on your players' (rather than the characters') own mystery solving skills to know how to determine when it is solved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T10:19:06-08:00","id":1052044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052039#post1052039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is going to come up more. Like with Aspirations, a lot of CofD 2e uses the idea that the players and the Storyteller are gathering to tell a story together. Not just that the players are there to react to the GM's story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have some advice here, and it is going to come in handy for the next section on Social Manuevering. Don't think of them as mini-games, don't stop and 'do an Investiagtion'. The Clues are the same as the narrative clues you had before, only this gives you a system to track how many clues the players have gathered and a system that doesn't just rely on your players' (rather than the characters') own mystery solving skills to know how to determine when it is solved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold one moment. I'm going to give you my thoughts on Social Maneuvering right now and then we can get right back to this argument. I don't hold back in this post and am very critical.<br /> <br /> <b>SOCIAL MANEUVERING</b><br /> <br /> My initial impressions are good. The text emphasises that social manuevering isn't mind control, which is good. However, the mention of \u201cDoors\u201d is another addition to the terminology that now at initial impression seems to be the \u201cClues\u201d of the social system. So \u2026 I want to convince the Guard that he should let me pass without interference. The storyteller determines that the Guard has Resolve or Composure 3, which gives him three \u201cdoors\u201d. He also has an aspiration to become employee of the month, which adds a fourth door.<br /> <br /> So I need to present him with four different arguments for him to let me through? \u201cYou're not paid enough to risk your life for this.\u201d (Door 1 unlocked). \u201cI promise to treat you to coffee if you let me through.\u201d (Door 2 unlocked). Ehm \u2026 \u201cI'm going to find your children and shoot them too if you don't let me pass!\u201d (Door 3 unlocked). Damnit, most people would have broken by now. \u201cEh! Could you let me pass, please?\u201d (Door 4 unlocked) Woohoo!<br /> <br /> Okay, if presented with a social action in game, my usual storytelling technique has been to evaluate the player's argument, decide how the target feels about the argument, decide whether or not he has any conflicting ideas, and have the character evaluate the possible consequences of either agreeing or disagreeing. Then the outcome of the player's roll determines the strength in which he presents this argument. There are a few steps to that too, but at least it's natural. I assume that the way I want to play this game too is for my player to present an argument and make a roll. If the roll is good and the argument is especially valid, then I would let the player succeed despite any amount of \u201cdoors\u201d in the way. If the target is especially defensive, then maybe I could use something similar to \u201cdoors\u201d to encourage my players to come up with additional arguments. I don't think I want to \u201climit myself to (Resolve or Composure)\u201d though. I'd go by feeling here, and what feels like it'd make sense.<br /> <br /> Okay, later on the book says that I can't just run the arguments in a row like that. I need different situations for different rolls with time in between depending on the impression the target has gotten of the character. That's unnecessary complexity. All of this should be written as storyteller advice with the only hard rule being \u201cuse common sense instead of relying too much on irrelevant elements such as impression level determining roll intervals.\u201d I don't want to play a computer game where I'm told to come back tomorrow for new daily quests. I want to either succeed or fail, and if I fail, I need to come up with a new approach. The system doesn't need all this other crap. At least not if it's going to be calling itself a storytelling system.<br /> <br /> I play Exalted 3E a lot and that system has a lot of crunch and a lot of fine little details that you need to take into consideration. Much of it is overly complex. However, it has a really good social influence system that focuses on what's actually important: storytelling, narrative flow, drama. I think I'm going to play social influence like that because it's easy to do in Chronicles of Darkness. You have the dice pools already. Now all you need to do is to focus on what makes sense, out of character and in character. You don't need to worry about completely irrelevant and immersion-breaking moments like \u201cyour impression level got hostile and will be so for a week now!\u201d Why a week? Well, the chart said so.<br /> <br /> I admit that this door opening system can be made to seem immersive and with narrative flow if the storyteller is properly prepared and has thought out every single door and various scenes in which the players can interact witht the target. I'm not saying that it doesn't work. All I'm saying is that it relies too heavily on charts and numbers to feel satisfying. A simple disclaimer about \u201cignore/change any of these rules if you feel that the players did something exceptional that should get them straight to the resolution\u201d would be enough to please me. Then I don't have to feel like I'm playing the game wrong if I want to focus more on storytelling and less on charts.<br /> <br /> <b>EXAMPLE OF SOCIAL MANUEVERING</b><br /> <br /> This is what I wanted to see. After my long rant, I want to be proven wrong. Let's see what it has to say.<br /> <br /> Well, decide if you want to spell it Erikson or Erickson. You can't have both. I prefer Eriksson.<br /> <br /> Okay, so Stacy is going to manipulate the poor Professor now instead of simply asking him if she can borrow the book. Fair enough. Sometimes you need to do that. She impresses him with her occult wisdom and opens Door #1. Now she needs to unlock three more doors for her mind control to win, but she needs more time for that. She needs to wait until the next day (for some reason not disclosed by anything other than a chart with a rule that says that she needs to do that).<br /> <br /> The next day, Stacy e-mails the Professor about something related to the book, but she failed. Now he hates her enough to penalize any of her social actions by 1. Shame on her for not checking her grammar before hitting send. Last night's efforts cannot save her from this. Alas, she must now wait for a week to try again. That's the time required for the Professor to get over this horrible mistake.<br /> <br /> So after a week of googling the poor Professor (she should have just broken into his library and stolen the book by now), she discovers that he wants to be a respected academic (it took her a week to google this, so she's not especially good at googling). She tells him that she has a friend who is good at ciphers and that they should totally get to read his book. She unlocks another door which in game makes the Professor (who still is disgruntled because of her bad grammar) slightly in her favor again but will still refuse to show her the book.<br /> <br /> After another week of googling, she figured out that he's vain. She blatantly lies about him with tears in her eyes to make him feel good about himself. This makes him like her again. She writes him a letter of thanks with an exceptional success (she not only corrected her grammar, but used thesaurus to seem more smart). Boom! Two doors open! The Professors lends her his book, unknowing of how much Stacy's player wanted to kill herself and her storyteller for putting up with this event.<br /> <br /> <b>Now, this is how I would have wanted to run this: </b><br /> <br /> Stacy impresses the Professor with her knowledge at the event (maybe through a good social roll as well as a roll connected to her Occult skill). This opens up a conversation with the Professor there at the event and I let the player try another approach. Stacy asks the Professor there and then if she can borrow the book, but she fails. Since the Professor has a good impression of Stacy, he laughs it off and says that he's reluctant to let anyone read it because of how valuable it is. After some conversation, Stacy's player makes a roll to profile the Professor and gains an understanding of how he wants to be respected. She tries a new, final approach, this time with a slight penalty, where she mentions her friends who's good with ciphers. This succeeds, which makes the storyteller deem the scene to have been progressive enough to let the Professor agree to show her the book. All was done in a single scene through creative roleplaying. If the Professor was more against it, then perhaps I'd want the player to rethink her strategy and try something new another day.<br /> <br /> <b>FORCING DOORS</b><br /> <br /> I agree with some of the things written here, like how a target can be immune to further efforts if you try to force it too hard and fail. <i>Hard Leverage </i>makes sense as a rule too, but I'd still ignore the \u201cdoors\u201d part and have it be relied entirely on the player's roleplay or the outcome of his roll. It's interesting how the example shows Stacy threaten the Professor at gunpoint and still only get through a single door. Hah! Now she needs to wait for a week to try to threaten him at gunpoint again.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've already spent a lot of money on this game now, and now I have read two major rules (Investigation and Social Maneuvering) which both gave me a bad taste in my mouth. I hope I won't regret my purchase and that I either don't understand how \u201cthis is good\u201d or that it can somehow be salvaged to better fit my way of storytelling. I was going to read the rest of the chapter today, but my thoughts on this social maneuvering part got so huge that I'll probably settle with this for now.<br /> <br /> I want to talk about everything in this post. I came at it hard, and I really wanted to be wrong about this one. If you use this system, could you provide some examples of how you've used it in game in ways that's been enjoyable and made sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T11:03:38-08:00","id":1052060,"title":"","content":"Social Manuevering isn't for the doorman, that can be dealt with in one roll. In the example given Stacy makes a good first impression so the professor is inclined to listen to her but then her email shows that she isn't as good as he first thought she was so he doesn't prioritise her anymore. The reason fails add a penalty to future rolls is that it gives you a reason to doubt that doing what that person wants may be a bad idea.<br /> As others have said both are optional and actually most of them were used in one splat core (the chase rules are from Werewolf I believe) and collected in CofD book when it came out. In other words most game lines will need to assume that you don't have access to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T11:48:50-08:00","id":1052078,"title":"","content":"I've been anticipating this one for a while. Social Maneuvering is, in my opinion, a great system that suffers from poor presentation, and if I ever have the time I would like to do an Actual Play focused on giving examples of how to use the SM system well. Everyone thinks it sounds overcomplicated and awful the first time they read it (I did too), but I think that's in part because the book really buries the lede in this section. The whole thing should have been presented in pretty much the opposite order.<br /> <br /> First of all, I think you misinterpreted Forcing Doors a little bit. Forcing Doors reduces the whole process to one single roll. The subject's doors apply as a penalty to the roll, and if it succeeds, all of the subject's doors open. This is, basically, the process you describe as being preferable, where the player makes their argument, you determine if a dice roll is necessary and if so, what dice pool they should roll based on their approach, and the results of the roll determine how successful the argument is in swaying the subject. Doors is just a flowery name for the difficulty of the Forcing Doors roll, and it's usually pretty easy to determine - it's just the lower of the subject's Resolve or Composure, + or - 1 depending on what's being asked of them and whether that would help them fulfill an aspiration or inflict a Breaking Point. That number becomes the penalty to the roll (you can also apply further situational penalties or bonuses if you like), on a success the PC convinces the subject, on a failure they don't, and can't try again.<br /> <i>(note: I house rule that a failed Forcing Doors roll makes the subject's impression of the PC drop to Hostile, rather than that they can never engage in Social Maneuvering wit them again)</i><br /> <br /> Now, the proximity discussion of Hard Leverage to the discussion of Forcing Doors leads many to assume that Forcing Doors is always about threatening the subject, but this is not the case. Forcing Doors is just about pressuring the subject to make a decision <i>right now</i>, which is what most single-roll Social actions are. Threatening the subject is one way to pressure them into immediate action, but it is not the only way. If the PC does use threats, however, they can apply any Hard Leverage they employ as an equipment bonus on the roll.<br /> <br /> Now, sometimes you have ample time to try to convince someone to do something, and you don't want to risk putting them off by pressuring them to act immediately. That's what the more in-depth system is for. Instead of Doors applying as a penalty to one roll, they become a number of successful rolls that must be achieved. The impression level sets the interval at which one can attempt to open a subject's Doors, and this is another place that trips people up, because they see that a Neutral Impression takes 1 week between rolls and assume most social actions will be at a neutral impression so it will take weeks or months to get anything done. But, impressions are very easy to raise. Going from Neutral to Good only requires a minimal effort to endear yourself to the subject, no roll required. Being well groomed and polite is probably enough. Raising from Good to Excellent requires a bit more effort, constituting a roll of some kind, maybe trying to impress the subject. The impression can also be raised by one level with a gift or bribe, also known as Soft Leverage, and Soft Leverage is the only way to raise an impression from Excellent to Perfect.<br /> <br /> In my games, most Social Maneuvering takes place at a Good or Excellent impression, though Perfect is not difficult to achieve if the players want it. 30-minute intervals for the roll is within the level of abstract time that many RPG conversations take place in, at least in my experience, so Excellent is often enough unless the players are in a hurry.<br /> <br /> So, here's what Social Maneuvering tends to look like in my games (Bear in mind, I go by the guideline that dice should only be rolled to when the outcome of an action is both uncertain and has consequences for failure). First, the players try to endear themselves to the subject. They might talk politely in character, compliment the subject, or describe how they are behaving that might impress the subject. If I feel their effort is enough to make the subject more amicable, I make a note that their Impression is Good. If they go to great lengths, I might also ask for a roll (dice pool determined based on the approach), and if it is successful, I make a note that their Impression is Excellent. If they give the subject some kind of Soft Leverage, I bump the Impression up by 1 and make note of that. Once the PCs have made their attempts to butter up the subject, they'll make their attempts to persuade them. I'll assess their approach to determine if a dice roll is needed, and if so, what kind of roll and what dice pool. If they are persuasive enough, the subject might just give them what they want - the outcome is not uncertain, so no dice rolls needed. If the subject is reluctant, I might ask for a roll. If the PCs are pressuring the subject, I'll ask them to make a roll with a penalty equal to the subject's Doors (which is usually around 1-3). Otherwise, I won't apply a penalty, and if they succeed I'll make note that they've opened one door. In any case, I'll respond in character as the subject to indicate the subject's reaction. For example, if their Impression is Perfect, they're interested in the PCs proposition but might still need some convincing. If their Impression is Excellent, they're considering it but might say they need a few minutes to consider, and I'll narrative-time those few minutes by. If their impression is Good or Neutral, they might say they'll think about it and get back to them later. If the PCs continue to push at a Good or Neutral impression, or if they're at Excellent and need an immediate answer rather than narrating through the next half-hour, I'll call for another roll, this time with a penalty equal to the remaining Doors (usually 1-2).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:00:55-08:00","id":1052083,"title":"","content":"The comment towards the end and the lack of color seems to mean tear into this completely, if I'm mistaken, sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052044#post1052044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So \u2026 I want to convince the Guard that he should let me pass without interference. The storyteller determines that the Guard has Resolve or Composure 3, which gives him three \u201cdoors\u201d. He also has an aspiration to become employee of the month, which adds a fourth door.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote the text: &quot;Social maneuvering is a system for applying persuasion and social pressure over time.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fast talking past a guard on-the-spot generally isn't what Opening Doors is normally for, skip to Forcing Doors or have some way to get to a perfect impression off the bat (which means you either planned this and researched the guard to know his Vice and and Aspiration to use against him, or have some sort of powers that allow you to do find that out in the moment). Or just don't use Social Maneuvering for every social roll, because that's not the intent of the system.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to slow befriend the guard for whatever you're up to, so when the time is right you can get past the guard, then you use Opening Doors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, if presented with a social action in game, my usual storytelling technique has been to evaluate the player's argument, decide how the target feels about the argument, decide whether or not he has any conflicting ideas, and have the character evaluate the possible consequences of either agreeing or disagreeing. </div> </div> </div>That is exactly the process of determining how many Doors a character has...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want to either succeed or fail, and if I fail, I need to come up with a new approach. </div> </div> </div>Sorry but this just strikes me as hypocritical. You can't except that there are game design points to having multiple successful rolls be useful for long term endeavors, and then call this &quot;crap.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're praising Ex3's social mechanics (which frequently require multiple successful roles to get a larger task done), but bashing this for following pretty much the same design ideas. How is building up impressions any different from using Instill actions until the target has a high enough Intimacy towards you that you can use a Persuade action on them, and then have to keep doing so until you've exhausted them of Decision Points?<br /> <br /> The only big difference here is that the CofD doesn't integrate a bunch of things in Intimacies to build these things off of, and instead the CofD just collects similar elements (Virtue, Vice, Aspirations) and factors them in as separate elements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The system doesn't need all this other crap. At least not if it's going to be calling itself a storytelling system. </div> </div> </div>This is bullshit and you know it. &quot;Calling itself a storytelling system means mechanics are bad!&quot; is not a functional point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't need to worry about completely irrelevant and immersion-breaking moments like \u201cyour impression level got hostile and will be so for a week now!\u201d Why a week? Well, the chart said so. </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect. If your impression gets hostile, the maneuvering attempt <b>fails</b> in a week unless you do something to improve your impression in the mean time or Force Doors. Getting into a hostile impression means the other person isn't listening to you any more and you need to repair that if you want to play nice.<br /> <br /> Is a week arbitrary? Sure. But how it is immersion breaking that you've pissed someone off and if you don't do something about that soon, your attempt to convince them to do you favor is going to fail (keeping in mind that it doesn't mean you can't start again even if that's an uphill climb).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All I'm saying is that it relies too heavily on charts and numbers to feel satisfying. </div> </div> </div>There's one chart.<br /> <br /> And numbers are how we play the game. You need a lot more substance than this to have a really salient criticism.<br /> <br /> The system relies on your reading the system and using the different parts for what they're supposed to do. Using normal Opening Doors in a Forcing Doors situation isn't the game's fault when it doesn't seem to work right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't have both. </div> </div> </div>Do you really want to get into a single typo?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now she needs to unlock three more doors for her mind control to win </div> </div> </div>Stop. You don't get to just label in mind control to support your rant without ever addressing how this suddenly became the case. When establishing the goal of the action the ST had to sign of on this being something that Stacy could reasonably accomplish with mundane persuasion and your own responses acknowledge that this is the case. Don't tell us you want to be proven wrong when you're not honestly following the example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (it took her a week to google this, so she's not especially good at googling) </div> </div> </div>Good thing the book doesn't actually say this was a matter of a Google search. That's another you adding shit to make it look bad strike.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After another week of googling,.. </div> </div> </div>Nope. Using an Aspiration to open a Door doesn't count as your action for that interval, it's a bonus on top of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Now, this is how I would have wanted to run this: </b> </div> </div> </div>Of course how you would have run it isn't a good example for the book because it fails to demonstrate various permutations. That's why the example has Stacy screw up and fail, to show what that looks like in the system.<br /> <br /> How you would have done it is possible in the system if you want it to be that simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Hard Leverage </i>makes sense as a rule too, but I'd still ignore the \u201cdoors\u201d part and have it be relied entirely on the player's roleplay or the outcome of his roll. It's interesting how the example shows Stacy threaten the Professor at gunpoint and still only get through a single door. Hah! Now she needs to wait for a week to try to threaten him at gunpoint again. </div> </div> </div>OK so strike three on the examples then.<br /> <br /> When Forcing Doors you only roll once with a penalty equal to the number of Doors. Using Hard Leverage removes Doors automatically. So Stacy didn't &quot;only open 1 door and have to wait a week.&quot; She reduced the Doors from 4 to 3, reducing the penalty on her roll from -4 to -3, making it that much easier for her to succeed (and she only needs one success) to get the book; and then deal with the consequences of having robbed Erickson at gunpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:03:19-08:00","id":1052085,"title":"","content":"TLDR of my previous post - Forcing Doors is your normal, one-roll Social action you'll want to use most of the time, Doors are a standardized way to determine the baseline difficulty of the roll, and all the rest of Social Maneuvering is a system for softening someone up before making the Forcing Doors roll to reduce the penalty, and if you have the luxury of enough time, you can even circumvent the Forcing Doors roll entirely if you reduce the penalty to 0. Also, don't forget that dice rolls should only be called for in the first place if there's a reasonable chance of success, a reasonable chance of failure, and consequences for failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:11:15-08:00","id":1052093,"title":"","content":"I have not used this system. Some things I'd like to point out though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicles of Darkness, Social Maneuvering</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social maneuvering is a system for applying persuasion<br /> and social pressure <b>over time</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Storyteller decides the prof could be persuaded to let this random student use his precious collection in a single scene, no need to do Social Maneuvering. Go with a more organic flow of events, as you described. <br /> <br /> For a character who is Cautious, has a valuable collection he is protective of, and likely has students bothering him for it all the time (maybe even other, more sinister, parties interested in &quot;acquiring&quot; it), maybe the one encounter at a party will not be enough without supernatural influence.<br /> This is where the system shines. It allows you to have a social character use their good side in a protracted scheme-y way. The series Revenge comes to mind - so many many Doors to start with.<br /> The several scenes/rolls of Social Maneuvering are the alternative to the several scenes/rolls of scouting out the place, getting gear, and trying to steal it, as it were.<br /> <br /> A longer social campaign is harder to organise in a flowing organic way, and the Doors are tools to see how successful the attempts at influence are in a cumulative way, until eventually the target has enough trust towards the PC, or is just relaxed enough around them, or convinced of the commitment of the PC, or a combination of those, to help them out with something they really didn't want to help out with at first. Players don't need to know about the Doors of the target, at most an evaluation (Composure+Empathy?) of the target's disposition towards them - suspicious, un/cooperative, cautious, helpful, sympathetic, situational goodies.<br /> <br /> I'd wager 90% of romantic comedies could be framed as a single Social Maneuvering sequence, with the goal of marriage or a committed relationship. <br /> <br /> The interval between influence attempts is the core of the system, but notice this can be modified by Soft Leverage, which should be taken advantage of for important situations. If you try to influence a person multiple times too quickly, there is the risk of appearing manipulative.<br /> <br /> Notice in the example how everything is actually quite seriously to Stacy's disadvantage: 3 and 4 in relevant attributes (not your average random NPC) , as well as the Virtue being against her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So \u2026 I want to convince the Guard that he should let me pass without interference. The storyteller determines that the Guard has Resolve or Composure 3, which gives him three \u201cdoors\u201d. He also has an aspiration to become employee of the month, which adds a fourth door.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a situation perfectly described by the Forcing Doors part. When waiting and subtlety aren't desired or possible - presumably one wants to enter now, not tomorrow or in a week. If Stacy's a Social girl, I'm sure she can manage a roll at -4 for those Doors. (3 in the relevant attribute, 4 in the relevant skill, maybe some tool/merit/specialty bonuses, extra if she plays to his Vice or Virtue).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:28:05-08:00","id":1052106,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that my posts in this thread are my initial impressions which I write down as I read the books. They remain uncensored and unedited. This means that what I write in the beginning of a paragraph may contradict what I write in a later paragraph. While I could go back and edit stuff I realize later in the text that I got wrong, I choose not to do that because it defeats the purpose of this thread.<br /> <br /> When I appear overly critical and make jokes, I do that while trying to process the information for the first time.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> And you have made some good points about the system and my lack of grasping it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 02-20-2017, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:34:06-08:00","id":1052111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052106#post1052106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to point out that my posts in this thread are my initial impressions which I write down as I read the books. They remain uncensored and unedited. This means that what I write in the beginning of a paragraph may contradict what I write in a later paragraph. While I could go back and edit stuff I realize later in the text that I got wrong, I choose not to do that because it defeats the purpose of this thread.<br /> <br /> When I appear overly critical and make jokes, I do that while trying to process the information for the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I appreciate you doing it that way. Makes for a more colorful read, and I think it's valuable to see newcomers 'first impressions unfiltered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:34:34-08:00","id":1052112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052085#post1052085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TLDR of my previous post - Forcing Doors is your normal, one-roll Social action you'll want to use most of the time, Doors are a standardized way to determine the baseline difficulty of the roll, and all the rest of Social Maneuvering is a system for softening someone up before making the Forcing Doors roll to reduce the penalty, and if you have the luxury of enough time, you can even circumvent the Forcing Doors roll entirely if you reduce the penalty to 0. Also, don't forget that dice rolls should only be called for in the first place if there's a reasonable chance of success, a reasonable chance of failure, and consequences for failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a fantastic summery that would probably help a lot of people understand the doors system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:49:19-08:00","id":1052121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1051612#post1051612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally a description about Beats and how they work. I'm not really sure why we need to call these mini-XP Beats when we can just call them XP and then increase the costs of everything by five.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Trivia time.<br /> <br /> This was actually briefly referenced in the original God-Machine supplement, but it looks like it didn't make it into CofD. In drama (particularly in Stanislavski's system and method acting), a beat is a unit of action -- a character has a realization, or changes her tactics in regard to what she wants. In short, it's a change or a turn in the script.<br /> <br /> Whether they <i>needed </i>to call them that is, of course, subjective; personally, I like the way it ties things back to theatre.<br /> <br /> Even more trivial: they're called <i>beats </i>as a metaphor for the script-as-music...or because of a particularly thick Russian accent trying to say the word &quot;bit&quot; in English","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-20-2017, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:45:07-08:00","id":1052165,"title":"","content":"<b>CHASES</b><br /> <br /> It seems pretty straight forward at the start. I realize quickly that chases don't just refer to vehicle chases, but can be applied to any kind of action that involves this kind of contested action. For example, tracking someone through the wood while that someone is actively trying to mislead the tracker. Chase! Trying to get the information from the target's database while the corporation's hackers are trying to track your location. Chase! Finishing your report on the corrupt politician before your rival reporter finishes his. Chase!<br /> <br /> I enjoy the examples with different edges providing chase modifiers. This is a chart I appreciate because it gives a good idea on how to use modifiers. Not sure about <b>Seizing the Edge</b>. Seems like that can be handled better than the provided example. I'd probably do something like seizing the edge through exceptional successes instead of playing guessing game for some reason unrelated to the action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>THE SOCIAL CHASE</b><br /> <br /> Told you it could be used for other stuff. It even gives an example to use it for Social Manuevering. Some social situations for sure. Interrogation, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>VIOLENCE</b><br /> <br /> Yay! Finally!<br /> <br /> The mention of the <i>Beaten Down Tilt </i>is a neat addition.<br /> <br /> I must admit that the title \u201cDown and Dirty Combat\u201d immediately grabbed my attention.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis system resolves the entire fight in a single roll.\u201d<br /> <br /> (O_O)<br /> <br /> I think it's good that this rule exists but I'd probably only use it if I believe the fight would be trivial or uninteresting for the players.<br /> <br /> It's interesting how it mentions that you almost are required to use Willpower to win fights. I guess it makes sense if the system really is as gritty as it seems, especially for poor mortals. Further paragraphs remind me to keep mooks weak. It makes sense for a gritty game. I imagine that I can easily buff some enemies if I want to give my players and even more difficult experience.<br /> <br /> The text continues to be fairly straightforward when it describes Initiative. It says that weapons have Initiative penalties. I guess I'll learn more about that when I see actual listed weapons. And the modifiers cap at 5 like normal.<br /> <br /> Delaying Actions and Surprise are straightforward as well. Hmm. So all close combat attacks use Strength and all distanced attacks use Dexterity. But the ranged combat using Firearms ignores the opponent's Defense. As of right now, it seems like all you need to hit a target with a gun is a single success. Shouldn't be too difficult when you get three dice from Willpower.<br /> <br /> Is there some kind of soak to mitigate damage?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">So as long as you haven't done your action yet, you can choose to dodge (if you have the highest initiative, then does that apply to the previous round in between your actions?). You double Defense, roll them as dice and apply them later on as modifiers to the attack roll. Since this is an element of chance, it can give more successes than your normal Defense, but it's unlikely to do so. It feels like quite an unreliable gamble unless there are other factors in play.</span><br /> <br /> Hmm, so you can actually apply a sort of Defense against Firearms if they are up in your face? Seems like a fairly good defense too since you add the weapon's Size + 1 to it.<br /> <br /> I like the <i>Combat Summary Chart</i>. That's something I'd want to print out.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">When mentioning <i>Shooting into Close Combat</i>, it says that the shooter gets penalties depending on the number of people she wants to avoid (with a higher penalty if someone is grappled). This penalty applies to the attack against the enemy, right? Does failure mean that she actually hits any of the targets she wants to avoid? Or is that really not an issue unless you botch?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I don't really understand what <i>Human Shields </i>mean when they say that \u201cunlike normal cover, the victim takes all of the damage from the attack\u201d. Does that mean that the victim is always damaged if you shoot, or can you actually succeed at shooting only the enemy target? What about if you get an exceptional success? Oh, and it mentioned \u201carmor\u201d so I guess that answered my question about soak.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Wait! I think I found the answer to this: <i>Specified Targets</i>. If my target has taken my wife hostage and I don't trust that there are any other safe ways than to make a shot, he will be considered in cover. My wife has Stamina 2 and Armor 1 which penalizes my attack by 3. Now if I would shoot, then my wife will also suffer the damage. But if I specify that the target is the bad guy's head, it says that I have a -3 penalty. This should allow me to shoot the bad guy in the head without harming my wife despite her being his hostage. I don't think the penalty would cap at 5 for this though, so it's probably at -6 \u2026 which is a difficult shot.</span><br /> <br /> <i>Tilts </i>are mentioned. I ordered a bunch of Tilt Cards from DrivethruRPG the other day without knowing what they were. Now I do. I'm glad I ordered them.<br /> <br /> Armor definitely seems like the life-saver here when you can't dodge firearms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>INJURY AND HEALING</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">You roll Stamina each round to remain conscious when your rightmost health box has been checked with bashing damage. However, is your Stamina penalized after every attempt or does it stay the same?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>SOURCES OF HARM</b><br /> <br /> I don't have much to say about this. It seemed straightforward.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>VEHICLES</b><br /> <br /> This is also fairly straightforward. Seeing all of the different modifiers is a bit intimidating, but not in a way that takes away from the experience. It makes sense for what it is and it contains enough meat to allow for creativity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EQUIPMENT</b><br /> <br /> The <i>Availability and Procurement </i>paragraph notes some good guidelines on how to deal with obtaining equipment.<br /> <br /> <br /> I noticed how I got a little distracted while reading <i>The Build Equipment Action </i>which made it difficult to absorb the information. I'm going to take a break because of that and get back to this section the next time. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:36:23-08:00","id":1052190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052044#post1052044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least not if it's going to be calling itself a storytelling system.</div> </div> </div> </div>To address this real quick, storytelling system, see 'system' is in there for a reason. It is providing a system for telling stories as a group. All the parts of the story have systems available. I personally love that there are systems for these things; for years I played DnD where their were all kinds of systems for fighting and magic and traps, but when it came to social things or solving puzzles and mysteries, the game said, whelp, that's on you folks cause we ain't gonna bother. Why is it ok for combat to have a 'complicated' system but not other parts of the story? As far as I can tell, its just an artifact of the old DnD crowd and has nothing to do with what makes a good game.<br /> <br /> Your comment about Down and Dirty Combat is telling here. 'Oh my god, there is combat where you resolve it in one roll!?' versus ' I want my social scenes resolved in one roll.' just doesn't make sense to me, even though that's how so many games have been for so long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052044#post1052044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold one moment. I'm going to give you my thoughts on Social Maneuvering right now and then we can get right back to this argument. I don't hold back in this post and am very critical.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, back to this. The same I said about Investigations is true. I don't run it as (nor think it should be run as): &quot;Alright first attempt, a week passes, second attempt&quot;. I run it as: &quot;OK last game you were talking to the professor about borrowing his book, then you went and explored that spooky mansion and got a bit hurt, you've rested up for a bit and while you were doing that thought about how best to approach the professor some more. It's been about a week since you initially asked him, do you want to follow up?&quot; Social maneuvering isn't a mini-game, its a tracking system for long term persuasion of people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052165#post1052165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">So as long as you haven't done your action yet, you can choose to dodge (if you have the highest initiative, then does that apply to the previous round in between your actions?). You double Defense, roll them as dice and apply them later on as modifiers to the attack roll. Since this is an element of chance, it can give more successes than your normal Defense, but it's unlikely to do so. It feels like quite an unreliable gamble unless there are other factors in play.</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you have the Highest Initiaitve then you would have to Delay Your Action to Dodge. Since you need them to attack you to Dodge.<br /> <br /> The success on the Dodge roll actually subtract Success from the attack roll not dice from the pool.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> I have a Defense of 2. Someone tries to punch me with a Strength + Brawl of 4. Normally that's a pool of 2. They roll and get 1 success, I take 1 Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> If I decide to Dodge instead. I roll 4 dice, lets say I get 2 success. Then they roll their full 4 dice pool and get 2 successes. But my Dodge success cancel those out (2-2=0) so I take no damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Added in a follow up to the not a mini-game discussion. 02-20-2017, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:41:51-08:00","id":1052197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052190#post1052190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your comment about Down and Dirty Combat is telling here. 'Oh my god, there is combat where you resolve it in one roll!?' versus ' I want my social scenes resolved in one roll.' just doesn't make sense to me, even though that's how so many games have been for so long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. My personal opinion is not so much wanting a super-simple social system, but rather wanting to avoid hiccups in roleplaying. In a combat situation, I'm okay with interrupting narrative for the sake of combat mechanics, but I don't feel the same in a social roleplaying situation. I'm also the kind of roleplayer who prefers social RP before combat RP. In fact, when I'm a player, I almost never play combat oriented characters. As an ST, I try to keep fights rare so that they are more dramatic when they eventually happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:51:54-08:00","id":1052206,"title":"","content":"I think the social and investigation system is something I need to try in order to fully appreciate. After reading your comments, I do recognize that the system can be used without it feeling forced, but I think that's something that will be requiring some experience playing with the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:56:21-08:00","id":1052209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052197#post1052197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point. My personal opinion is not so much wanting a super-simple social system, but rather wanting to avoid hiccups in roleplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I guess I didn't go into this explcitly before, but there is a very strong design decision with Chronicles of Darkness that the old 'roleplaying vs rollplaying' argument is garbage. Roleplaying is what happens when I sit down to the table to play, start to finish. Whether I am talking about my character, talking in-character (something I almost never do myself), rolling dice, not rolling dice, listening to the Storyteller talk; all of it is roleplaying. The dice are there to faciliate roleplaying, if the outcome of an action is uncertain and important, then you use dice to help determine it. Thats how this game is designed, not that 'roleplaying' means acting in-character and anything out of character is something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052197#post1052197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a combat situation, I'm okay with interrupting narrative for the sake of combat mechanics, but I don't feel the same in a social roleplaying situation. I'm also the kind of roleplayer who prefers social RP before combat RP. In fact, when I'm a player, I almost never play combat oriented characters. As an ST, I try to keep fights rare so that they are more dramatic when they eventually happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to play not combat characters too, and I damn well want there to be as much of a system there for me to use as there is for the combat characters.<br /> <br /> Also, I edited the previous post while you were responding. I'll re-post it here though:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Ekorren</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052044#post1052044\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Hold one moment. I'm going to give you my thoughts on Social Maneuvering right now and then we can get right back to this argument. I don't hold back in this post and am very critical.</span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, back to this. The same I said about Investigations is true. I don't run it as (nor think it should be run as): &quot;Alright first attempt, a week passes, second attempt&quot;. I run it as: &quot;OK last game you were talking to the professor about borrowing his book, then you went and explored that spooky mansion and got a bit hurt, you've rested up for a bit and while you were doing that thought about how best to approach the professor some more. It's been about a week since you initially asked him, do you want to follow up?&quot; Social maneuvering isn't a mini-game, its a tracking system for long term persuasion of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  fixed a quote 02-20-2017, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:09:10-08:00","id":1052216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052165#post1052165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">So as long as you haven't done your action yet, you can choose to dodge (if you have the highest initiative, then does that apply to the previous round in between your actions?). You double Defense, roll them as dice and apply them later on as modifiers to the attack roll. Since this is an element of chance, it can give more successes than your normal Defense, but it's unlikely to do so. It feels like quite an unreliable gamble unless there are other factors in play.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The successes from a Dodge roll subtract not from the attacker's roll, but from their <i>rolled successes</i>. You're right that it's a riskier maneuver because of the chancy nature of the dice, but it's far more likely than straight applying your Defense to be able to result in not taking damage at all from an attack.<br /> <br /> Dodge replaces any non-reflexive actions for that round. If you're at the top of initiative, then you can Dodge for this round, regardless of what happened last round, but only if you take no other standard action with your turn. If you're at the top of initiative and throw an attack, then somebody else uses their turn to attack you, you no longer have the option of Dodging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052165#post1052165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I don't really understand what <i>Human Shields </i>mean when they say that \u201cunlike normal cover, the victim takes all of the damage from the attack\u201d. Does that mean that the victim is always damaged if you shoot, or can you actually succeed at shooting only the enemy target? What about if you get an exceptional success? Oh, and it mentioned \u201carmor\u201d so I guess that answered my question about soak.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>When you take cover behind a wall, it reduces incoming damage by its Durability, and any remaining damage is dealt to both you and the wall. When you take cover behind a person, you take damage reduced by the person's effective Durability as cover as detailed there, but the person takes the full damage, unreduced.<br /> <br /> Your judgment with called shots to try to avoid shooting the hostage is pretty sound, yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052165#post1052165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">You roll Stamina each round to remain conscious when your rightmost health box has been checked with bashing damage. However, is your Stamina penalized after every attempt or does it stay the same?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It stays the same, and wound penalties do not apply to this roll. It's bad enough that you're stuck with the risk of failure recurring every turn, on a small one-trait pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 02-20-2017, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:20:08-08:00","id":1052254,"title":"","content":"As others have mentioned Dodging is kind of chancy but an average roll will prevent more damage than your base defense would. Plus there are merits later on that will allow you to perform a counter as part of a dodge action.<br /> <br /> Armor soak does exist and it's <i>really</i> powerful. A suit of riot gear is the difference between a guy with a hand cannon dealing 4 lethal and that same guy dealing a single bashing. Wearing riot gear is obviously not something you can get away with in a lot of settings but armor is something you'll always want when the shooting starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T18:21:24-08:00","id":1052319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052190#post1052190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have the Highest Initiaitve then you would have to Delay Your Action to Dodge. Since you need them to attack you to Dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this how other people interpret this rule? Huh. I've always just allowed players to declare a Dodge at any time, and doing so forfeits their action the next time their Initiative comes up, even if that's technically in the next round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T18:26:47-08:00","id":1052324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052319#post1052319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this how other people interpret this rule? Huh. I've always just allowed players to declare a Dodge at any time, and doing so forfeits their action the next time their Initiative comes up, even if that's technically in the next round.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally incline away from allowing a Dodge for somebody who's already used their action that round, to give it a little timing significance (combat rounds being very fast little flashpoints), but I don't think there's a point in bothering with delay action rules. Pre-emptively initiating a Dodge at the beginning of a turn you expect to be attacked a bunch of times in is fine, and doesn't need any extra bookkeeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T19:02:58-08:00","id":1052340,"title":"","content":"Forcing people to delay is also kind of harsh because it means permanently reducing your Initiative for the fight. It makes Dodging if you're going first very suspect if you have to delay until your attacked and can be sent to the bottom of the list if people avoid you more than you expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T01:28:42-08:00","id":1052451,"title":"","content":"Ugh. Social Maneuvering. I don't have time to dissect your post right now, so I'm going to give a really quick response rather than write (another; see signature) essay, which may fall afoul of your &quot;my understanding changes through the course of this post&quot; shtick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052044#post1052044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial impressions are good. The text emphasises that social manuevering isn't mind control, which is good. However, the mention of \u201cDoors\u201d is another addition to the terminology that now at initial impression seems to be the \u201cClues\u201d of the social system. So \u2026 I want to convince the Guard that he should let me pass without interference. The storyteller determines that the Guard has Resolve or Composure 3, which gives him three \u201cdoors\u201d. He also has an aspiration to become employee of the month, which adds a fourth door.<br /> <br /> So I need to present him with four different arguments for him to let me through? \u201cYou're not paid enough to risk your life for this.\u201d (Door 1 unlocked). \u201cI promise to treat you to coffee if you let me through.\u201d (Door 2 unlocked). Ehm \u2026 \u201cI'm going to find your children and shoot them too if you don't let me pass!\u201d (Door 3 unlocked). Damnit, most people would have broken by now. \u201cEh! Could you let me pass, please?\u201d (Door 4 unlocked) Woohoo!</div> </div> </div> </div>ARGH. There is so much wrong with this interpretation already. Here's the thing. Social Maneuvering is not a replacement for persuasion, intimidation, or any other straight-up talk-to-the-guy. If you want to convince a guard to let you past, you shouldn't use Social Maneuvering. There's no time, unless this is step 2 of a 14 step process for heist preparation. (Which, y'know, is cool. Watch Ocean's Eleven and how they acquire the technician's badge. Make sure you rewind and see how they <i>find out</i> his personal information.)<br /> <br /> ElvesofZion has already said it better than I have time to, but just to reiterate: I would advise against using Investigation or Social Maneuvering for anything fast. Do other stuff in between relevant rolls: that's what they're <i>good</i> for. Unless your task makes sense in that context, I would, again, advise against using those two systems because they're built around <i>having time</i>.<br /> <br /> And as Charlaquin implied, this isn't really your fault. Most people seem to make this mistake with the system. I'd really like to see them take another pass at explaining it and expanding it at some point because, as is, it's clearly really confusing for most people.<br /> <br /> So... no. You shouldn't present the guard with four arguments. (Actually, if you're going that route, you'd better have a 6th and 7th because each of these is a roll, which might fail.) First, you should improve the guard's impression of you. You should make an Empathy roll, or read his mind to discover his Vice, or whatever. Considering Impressions is important! Because without it, you don't understand the <i>time</i> aspect of the system. You breezed <i>right</i> over this fundamental bit and it hurts your ability to understand what's going on.<br /> <br /> Then, you figure out a general plan of attack. Maybe you &quot;accidentally&quot; bump into him at the bar. I... look, guards are hard, because the correct story-thing to do with a guard is to one-shot him and move on. Mooks exist to make the hero look competent, not to present a challenge. Digressing. But you should be using what you learn at each successive Door as a prelude to the next. Oh, you chat him up at the bar and learn he's got kids. Then maybe you help him get a present for his kid's birthday coming up. Maybe it's a bike, so you tell him of a good bike trail. Or you find out he wants to be employee of the month and you give him some tips on how to move up the corporate ladder. I... he's a guard! Guards don't--. Agh.<br /> <br /> Again, you open Doors by rolling stat+skill. If you're rolling the exact same combination every time then, as a player, you're pretty one-trick and one-dimensional. Hell, show him some fancy karate moves with some Presence+Brawl or something, at least, I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T01:49:42-08:00","id":1052455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052451#post1052451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh. Social Maneuvering. I don't have time to dissect your post right now, so I'm going to give a really quick response rather than write (another; see signature) essay, which may fall afoul of your &quot;my understanding changes through the course of this post&quot; shtick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to read your essay after I've finished the readthrough. As you call it, my &quot;shtick&quot; is to show my first impressions however flawed they may be. Let's leave Social Manuevering for now. I'll get back to it when I'm done with the book. When I've read and digested everything, I'm going to get back to things like that and clear up everything I've misunderstood about the system later. If I still can't wrap my head around it when I'm done, we can continue this discussion then.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I'm still confused about &quot;human shields&quot; and my example of &quot;using my wife as a shield&quot;. The more I think about it, would that situation be more of a &quot;shooting someone in a grapple&quot; rather than &quot;shooting someone with a human shield&quot;. I just want to figure out how to best kill the target without harming the hostage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T02:03:38-08:00","id":1052462,"title":"","content":"Probably too late to the party but here's my impressions. I'm aware of your style on your posts and want to add to the conversation how I'd treat each hurdle you found so far. I'll continue to address your following posts in this matter to help you grasp the system better.<br /> <br /> Re: I'm under the impression <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> is mistaken. An individual bonuses and/or penalties has a cap of +5/-5 (barring supernatural mitigating circumstances, but you're a mortal here). If you somehow manage to stack 2 bonuses, say, a +4 suit for the red carpet to appear sharp before the cameras and burning willpower for the +3 bonus on that but you haven't slept because of heavy coke abuse in the last 24 hours (-1), then you'll roll Presence+Socialize at +6 in order to become the People's magazine cover. Trying to surf a tsunami while there's a typhoon going on would be Dexterity+Athletics at -10 (-5 from wild waters, -5 from the uprooting trees wind velocity).<br /> <br /> Re: Contested actions tie: Roll again. Eventually someone's gonna win, even if that specific turn grappling each other was spent with them locking knuckles and grunting while facing one another in a dramatic fashion without anyone getting the upper hand, yet.<br /> <br /> Re: Time. I personally love saying &quot;Alright people, let's finish this chapter.&quot; When we've played a lot and the climax is starting to build.<br /> <br /> Re: It's called a beat instead of silly D&amp;Desque XPs as in &quot;story beats&quot;, an exercise in screen-writting. They mark the dramatic moments within scripts. Which is why 5 beats means 1 experience: you keep upping the ante into a climatic experience. Language is powerful.<br /> <br /> Re: No hard answers - nothing says you have to outright inquire, out of character which clues they're getting... just how they're looking for them. That should inform what to give them.<br /> <br /> Can your players solve everything by having your characters passively go about collecting clues? Yes, if you don't introduce complications you can. That's how the horror happens, that's how the drama splits forth, that's how they earn beats and experience.<br /> <br /> Re: Librarian example: Then your characters, in desperation at the oblivious librarian do something drastic: such as taking her hostage. Drama and beats galore. Or someone's savvy enough to social maneuver that without a hitch, but I wouldn't give the guy time to take the librarian out on a date to get a better impression before the Horror strikes. Or maybe the Librarian was the Horror and that's why she was so adamant. Go nuts.<br /> <br /> Re: \u201cYou're not paid enough to risk your life for this.\u201d Could be heavy leverage (Presence or Strength+Intimidation). Just score 1 success whilst penalized by his 4 doors and he'll back away.<br /> <br /> Social maneuvering is specifically tailored at long term discussions. Like making a pro-life minister realize that sometimes a woman needs to have an abortion (73% of people agree with this, sometimes there's mitigating circumstances according to John Oliver).<br /> <br /> Re: Stacy failing at getting the last door with a threat at gunpoint and waiting a week to threaten him again (forcing doors and accruing no successes). Stacy now takes a breaking point for the threat and can shot the idiot in the leg at a bonus on however much damage she pulled, and another breaking point. And she gets I don't know, like 3 beats and 2 conditions for more beats after all is said and done.<br /> <br /> Maybe she scores 5 successes. Add 2 from the gun and she hit the femoral artery. He's going to die unless somebody provides <i>expert </i>medical care within turns. Maybe she doesn't cares, and just grabs the key to the private section and goes for the book. Maybe she does that before trying to desperately re-arrange the murder-scene somehow. The drama is flowing, the players are having cold sweat and the beats are mounting. People is having fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 02-21-2017, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T02:32:53-08:00","id":1052469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052455#post1052455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still confused about &quot;human shields&quot; and my example of &quot;using my wife as a shield&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can do this, but surely using your own wife would BIG penalty on Breaking Point for that ( like -4 or -5 even, depends on your relation with spouse ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052455#post1052455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I think about it, would that situation be more of a &quot;shooting someone in a grapple&quot; rather than &quot;shooting someone with a human shield&quot;. I just want to figure out how to best kill the target without harming the hostage.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, shooting in to close combat gives you -2 penalty for each participants you <i>do not want to hit</i> ( i.e. 'your side' characters ).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T04:12:01-08:00","id":1052489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052216#post1052216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When you take cover behind a wall, it reduces incoming damage by its Durability, and any remaining damage is dealt to both you and the wall. When you take cover behind a person, you take damage reduced by the person's effective Durability as cover as detailed there, but the person takes the full damage, unreduced.<br /> <br /> Your judgment with called shots to try to avoid shooting the hostage is pretty sound, yeah.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It stays the same, and wound penalties do not apply to this roll. It's bad enough that you're stuck with the risk of failure recurring every turn, on a small one-trait pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth's noting that when using cover*, firearm in question needs to have Weapon Rating bigger than durability of your cover - if it doesn't, it can't damage you, no matter how many successes you roll. Hugging the cover is really, really good defense measure against typical personal weapons that rarely go above Weapon Rating 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> *not necessarily a human shield","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:56:30-08:00","id":1052572,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> , I forgot that Delay is permanent. Looking at it again, I also thought it said Dodge was a Reflexive action in response to an Attack, but it's not. It just says anytime before your action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1052319#post1052319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this how other people interpret this rule? Huh. I've always just allowed players to declare a Dodge at any time, and doing so forfeits their action the next time their Initiative comes up, even if that's technically in the next round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it more, I actually run it where it can be declared before the first action still and its just takes that turns action anyway. My point was that I don't allow it to count the previous or next turns action slot. You have to choose each turn if you Dodge or not, although I can see your way would work too. I actually have lots of different thoughts on how I would prefer Initiative but have just gone with the above as a RAW from the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Clarified an ambiguous pronoun 02-21-2017, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:02:06-08:00","id":1052967,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar482_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"482\" data-vbnamecard=\"482\">Ekorren</a> I like this, I hadn't thought of this type of post and am really enjoying the read. Now that I'm caught up I'm looking forward to responding to future posts ^.^<br /> <br /> (side note, I wish I could do this but due to sneak peaks, forum speculation, and dev blogs i'm almost never blind when going into a new CofD book, le sigh.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T11:45:39-08:00","id":1055327,"title":"","content":"I've been a bit busy but let's get back to this. I also have my physical copy now, by the way. This will be a shorter read.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>BUILDING EQUIPMENT</b><br /> <br /> It's interesting that what I thought was going to be a crafting system also includes other forms of \u201ccreations,\u201d like organizations and plans.<br /> <br /> Ah, so it's supposed to be a McGyver system of sorts, where you \u201cjury rig\u201d together stuff while under duress or where you just create simpler stuff. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">When it asks if I have \u201cdots in the relevant Skill equal to the equipment bonus blahdiblah,\u201d does it refer to the Skill which the equipment boosts or the Skill I use to craft the object?</span><br /> <br /> The actual crafting action seems straightforward. You get a penalty depending on the equipment bonus and then you roll and hope you're lucky. If you're crafting in combat, it takes a number of turns equal to the equipment bonus.<br /> <br /> The good thing about the examples of play is that they remind you of rules that you easily forget as you read. For example, that you earn Beats for resolving Conditions. The example for crafting a plan was interesting. You can boost your pools fairly easily by coming prepared (and not fucking up).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FICTION: YEVGENY</b><br /> <br /> What is this? Google translate? This must be the worst written text I have read in a while. Did Onyx Path pay for this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>BLACK THREADS: STORYTELLING</b></span><br /> <br /> \u201c<i>Some groups find it ideal to stick with one Storyteller throughout the course of a chronicle ...\u201d</i> That's the way I'm playing and the perspective I'll have when reading this. Any other way doesn't fit my particular playstyle or the group I'm playing with.<br /> <br /> I have some ideas of the kind of a campaign I'd run, but I'm withholding any decisions until I've read all of the book. I also want to take a look at the God-Machine Chronicle to see what that is about.<br /> <br /> Most of the listed Storytelling Responsibilities are natural because of how long I've been roleplaying, but it's good that they exist. Let's see if there is any new advice that I could benefit from right away.<br /> <br /> <b>Provide Space to Play: </b>We have two spaces that we play in. Most of the time we're playing over at a friend's place, but occassionally we're at mine. I have a better setup for managing atmospheric music and such, but my friend has a bit more space.<br /> <br /> <b>Food and Drink: </b>We usually eat lunch together before we play, then buy some snacks for the game. Then we play for a couple of hours (usually 5-6 hours). When we don't have time to eat before the game, we usually take a break a few hours in to order pizza.<br /> <br /> <b>Establishing Setting and Theme: </b>I think all players know fairly well what the others are interested in. We usually leave this to the Storyteller and then run with what he comes up with.<br /> <br /> <b>Interesting Characters: </b>Every player is certaintly different when it comes to this. I rarely play combat monkey and usually plays either the sneaky type, the smart type or the social type. One of my players always play chaotic neutral and his characters tend to be cruel even when I want to have a more heroic group (I have to compromise with him a lot). Another player can play any type of character concept, but is often fairly passive and laid back. He can take some clever initiatives, but he often lets other players shine. He seems to enjoy playing the silent strong guy who stands next to the social character and looks menacing. Another of my players is very hyperactive and likes to take the spotlight. He doesn't care about optimization and usually creates very poorly made characters because he has an idea in his head and thinks it'd be fun, even if it doesn't work in practice.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheerlead for the Player Characters: </b>I agree with this. I never go out of my way to punish my players and I often give more than I take. One of my players coined the phrase \u201cCIFA moment\u201d though. It came up some years ago when Spartacus was popular on TV and Batiatus had his quote about <a href=\"https://youtu.be/ruyWq7URlN0\" target=\"_blank\">\u201ccocks in fucking ass.\u201d</a> The CIFA moments are moments when I've taken all of my players hope and they think that they will be screwed over.<br /> <br /> <b>Providing Regalia: </b>I suck at this. I mostly ST Exalted where it's easy for players to jump ropes with the storythread. The regalia is usually some kind of important letter or a symbol that's supposed to mean something. I would like to do this more often.<br /> <br /> The <b>Spines </b>are all solid advice. It also gave some inspiration. Still not talking about any potential stories I'll run though.<br /> <br /> I find that there aren't too much for me to comment on here. Most of it are solid advice. Other things don't fit my prefered way of Storytelling. The <b>Exquisite Corpse</b> thing doesn't interest me at all.<br /> <br /> I don't have much experience with Storytelling horror. I've done some supernatural noir back in the day, and I've had grotesque and suspenseful elements in other games, mainly fantasy ones. Though I've played in horror games, I haven't really aimed to ST them, and this will be an interesting experience. If I can create a tense atmosphere for my players remain to be seen.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to continue with <b>Missing Persons: Creating Your Setting </b>next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:21:50-08:00","id":1055364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1055327#post1055327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it asks if I have \u201cdots in the relevant Skill equal to the equipment bonus blahdiblah,\u201d does it refer to the Skill which the equipment boosts or the Skill I use to craft the object?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Skill you use to craft the object.<br /> <br /> Side note: I love the building equipment system so much. Most RPGs make their crafting systems so complex and overwrought. CofD cuts it down to a single roll, and says it happens in the time between scenes or chapters, unless you want to Jury Rig something, in which case you get it now but the stakes are increased (a success on Jury Rigging has the same result as a failure on Building Equipment normally, etc.) And there are even rules baked right into the system telling you to skip the roll if there is no pressure, which makes them nicely new-GM-proof. Briliant system, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:19:03-08:00","id":1056183,"title":"","content":"<b>MISSING PERSONS: CHOOSE YOUR SETTING</b><br /> <br /> I understand that it's a really good tool for new Storytellers but I'm having some difficulties being interested at I start reading this. Thinking objectively, I do think it gives solid advice to new Storytellers and it's almost a walkthrough to how you can set up your first game.<br /> <br /> The methods where the Storyteller and the player design the game together doesn't appeal to me on either side of the table. When I'm Storyteller, I want to present the setting for my players. When I'm a player, I want to immerse myself in a world where I don't know what lurks around the corner. I blatantly ignore any suggestions in this chapter that doesn't fit my own playstyle---but I appreciate that it's there for others.<br /> <br /> The suggestions for how to create this \u201cmissing person\u201d could be applied to pretty much any NPC though. It presents some questions you could ask in order to better define the character which is a good way to add depth to NPCs. The part about <b>Putting it on Paper </b>is a good way to create NPCs that are somehow tied to player backgrounds. I do allow my players to design NPCs during the chargen process---I just don't want them to narrate the world around themselves in game. I want their focus to be on their own characters in a situation presented to them.<br /> <br /> As I was reading through <b>Implications</b>, a thought occurred to me that these \u201cmissing person\u201d rules can be used to present a situation where the person itself isn't missing per se, but the mystery itself needs to be uncovered. Your character wakes up in a rundown apartment covered in your boyfriend's blood and with his lifeless body next to you (boyfriend = missing person). You only remember a few vague details and you don't know if he was killed by you or someone else. Because everything implies that you're guilty, you dispose of the body and don't call the police. The mystery of \u201cfinding the missing person\u201d is then played out as you \u201cfinding the clues that eventually lead to the conclusion of what happened to him.\u201d The paranoia itself could be the horror of this story. Perhaps you gain breaking points when seeing cameras and police cars? Maybe you assault an innocent person because you think he's been watching you. You'll get breaking points if you see him without acting on it (because it adds to the paranoia) and you get breaking points for assaulting him and learning that he's innocent. I could truly torture my players with this. Hopefully in a good way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FICTION: MIRROR</b><br /> <br /> Oooh. I liked this. Very suspenseful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>HORROR AND WONDERS: ANTAGONISTS</b></span><br /> <br /> The book mentions <i>Ephemera </i>as ghosts of the dead, spirits of Shadow and angels of the God-Machine. I still don't know what the God-Machine is but I'm getting closer to it. By the way, I'm digressing a little now but I told a friend of mine that I was reading this book. He started whining about how it was \u201cthe worst system ever\u201d and how he \u201crefused to play after 30 minutes\u201d and how his \u201cvampire had no chance against a guard with a club.\u201d I told him that he probably sucked because the system seems generally well-liked. Or where there bigger issues with the \u201cpre-2E\u201d versions that came out some years ago? I consider only purchasing 2E versions if that's the case. Then I need to wait for Hunter for a while.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to it! Hopefully I understand the rules well enough to get into this antagonists now. I haven't made a test character yet so I'm not sure exactly how strong/weak new characters are in comparison.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Is the Initiative Modifier supposed to supplement the \u201cDexterity + Composure\u201d roll? So when the Cocky Mob Hitman has Initiative Modifier +7, I roll 8 dice, minus whatever penalty he may have from the weapon I've given him? Is Defense the rolled trait or am I actually supposed to remove seven dice from the attack roll if the target has Defense 7? Feels like a lot. I mean, sure, there are some with Defense 3 only who aren't supposed to be as good fighters.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EPHEMERAL BEINGS</b><br /> <br /> Another reference to the God-Machine. What does it mean when people begin to see its gears? Don't tell me.<br /> <br /> It was a cool piece of lore about what the ephemeral beings are and how they interact with the world. I still have no idea what anything referencing the God-Machine actually means though, but apparently you need to construct railway and dig pipes for angels to appear \u2026 or am I misunderstanding what they mean by infrastructure? Don't tell me. I want to experience the God-Machine stuff on my own.<br /> <br /> There are apparently a shit ton of ghosts around. There is an Underworld of sorts in this world and the doors leading to it are like ghosts themselves. Ghosts can become super ghosts if they hang around in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The shadow world is a reflection of the real world, since all things that exist is reflected there. Kind of like Stranger Things. So in the shadow world, spirits are born next to the reflections of furniture and cars and stuff, and then they fight each other and such. Well, most of them are floaty blobs since there probably isn't much essence around Uncle Tim's old vespa. Now, if the floaty blob hanging around Uncle Tim's old vespa should grow into a spirit worthy of that vespa, it needs to be exposed to essence, but the essence doesn't need to directly correlate to the old vespa---it's enough to be close enough to the vespa for it to pick up on some energy?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">So let's say that Uncle Tim got the old vespa on his fifteenth birthday, and his first girlfriend rode on its back when he took her up on Love Mountain and got to touch her boob. He kept this vespa in his garage for years, sometimes talking to it as he kept it nice and tidy. After some years, almost all parts of the vespa had been changed for new parts, but it was still the same old vespa and Tim still talked to it at times. When he had to sell it, he cried, and when his niece found it for him on an auction twenty years later, he cried again. Uncle Tim's love for the old vespa has charged it with essence for years, and the spirit has gone from a floaty blob to a self-aware and very active spirit who is now eager to eat other spirits. Does Uncle Time have a spirit? Has it been eaten by the vespa?</span><br /> <br /> Apparently the God-Machine thing is here in the material world, built from mechanisms hidden from sight by guile and magic. I've learned something new, but I'm equally confused. Hmm. Really? So this is an \u201cactual machine\u201d of sorts, but also not. More like if Cthulhu's home dimension had sex with a grandfather clock. I'm not really sure what its definition of \u201cInfrastructure\u201d is, but it seems like this God-Machine is this game's version of a \u201cgod.\u201d I assume that it doesn't go with the typical \u201cChristian-based\u201d supernatural story that's common in Western media. It takes elements from many mythologies and adds this God-Machine to represent a god-like entity. Don't tell me if I'm right, but you can tell me if I'm hot or cold.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to close down this reading session early today too because I'm tired from work. Will get to<b> Game Systems </b>next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 02-28-2017, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:54:34-08:00","id":1056208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Is the Initiative Modifier supposed to supplement the \u201cDexterity + Composure\u201d roll? So when the Cocky Mob Hitman has Initiative Modifier +7, I roll 8 dice, minus whatever penalty he may have from the weapon I've given him? Is Defense the rolled trait or am I actually supposed to remove seven dice from the attack roll if the target has Defense 7? Feels like a lot. I mean, sure, there are some with Defense 3 only who aren't supposed to be as good fighters.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Initiative isn't actually determined by a dice pool, it is an odd man out in the system. You roll a single d10, then add the Initiative Modifier to the value rolled, and then that sum is the character's base initiative for the encounter. So if you roll a 4 on the die and your initiative is +7, you've got initiative 11. You then apply whatever penalty for weapons drawn, so if you draw a -1 initiative knife on the first turn, then from the second turn on you're acting at initiative 10.<br /> <br /> Defense is not rolled unless you're Dodging. Defense 7 is indeed a lot. Don't forget the ability to spend Willpower on dice. Violence in CofD basically expects you to bleed Willpower as much as you can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">So let's say that Uncle Tim got the old vespa on his fifteenth birthday, and his first girlfriend rode on its back when he took her up on Love Mountain and got to touch her boob. He kept this vespa in his garage for years, sometimes talking to it as he kept it nice and tidy. After some years, almost all parts of the vespa had been changed for new parts, but it was still the same old vespa and Tim still talked to it at times. When he had to sell it, he cried, and when his niece found it for him on an auction twenty years later, he cried again. Uncle Tim's love for the old vespa has charged it with essence for years, and the spirit has gone from a floaty blob to a self-aware and very active spirit who is now eager to eat other spirits. Does Uncle Time have a spirit? Has it been eaten by the vespa?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Human beings don't have spirits in the Shadow Realm. Non-human animals, objects, places, emotions, ideas, yes, but not Tim himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:58:46-08:00","id":1056211,"title":"","content":"Ninja's by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Is the Initiative Modifier supposed to supplement the \u201cDexterity + Composure\u201d roll? So when the Cocky Mob Hitman has Initiative Modifier +7, I roll 8 dice, minus whatever penalty he may have from the weapon I've given him?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>So, Initiative is a weird one. Dex + Comp is not a dice pool, its the Initiative Modifier. You roll for initiative by rolling 1 die and adding the modifier to it (you also account for weapons). Only thing in the system like this that I know of.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Is Defense the rolled trait or am I actually supposed to remove seven dice from the attack roll if the target has Defense 7? Feels like a lot. I mean, sure, there are some with Defense 3 only who aren't supposed to be as good fighters.</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You subtract it from the attackers die pool. 7 dice for a defense of 7, yeah. Although, remember if you hit 0 or lower you get a Chance Die. When you Dodge then you double the pool and roll it, subtracting success from the attackers success (not their pool).<br /> <br /> Defense 3 is about average for most mortal enemies that I throw at my players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">So let's say that Uncle Tim got the old vespa on his fifteenth birthday, and his first girlfriend rode on its back when he took her up on Love Mountain and got to touch her boob. He kept this vespa in his garage for years, sometimes talking to it as he kept it nice and tidy. After some years, almost all parts of the vespa had been changed for new parts, but it was still the same old vespa and Tim still talked to it at times. When he had to sell it, he cried, and when his niece found it for him on an auction twenty years later, he cried again. Uncle Tim's love for the old vespa has charged it with essence for years, and the spirit has gone from a floaty blob to a self-aware and very active spirit who is now eager to eat other spirits. Does Uncle Time have a spirit? Has it been eaten by the vespa?</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Humans don't have a spirit directly no, and it is a purposeful left open mystery of the setting as to why. Emotions do generate and feed spirits though. So the love Uncle Tim feels could have a Spirit reflection in the form of a Spirit of Love.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't tell me if I'm right, but you can tell me if I'm hot or cold.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say maybe a bit hotter than warm but not hot. You have the right setting tone but are making some faulty assumptions about the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Ninja'd by @StupidLoserman 02-28-2017, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:40:44-08:00","id":1056246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't tell me if I'm right, but you can tell me if I'm hot or cold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Warmish, as Elves said, but even then, the game / setting leave a lot of it up to the Storyteller (the God-Machine is a tool, not a directive). Its true nature is ambiguous...Clarke's third law applies, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:12:24-08:00","id":1056293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056246#post1056246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Warmish, as Elves said, but even then, the game / setting leave a lot of it up to the Storyteller (the God-Machine is a tool, not a directive). Its true nature is ambiguous...Clarke's third law applies, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was going in with the assumption that 'you' were using the God-Machine and its attendent setting as written. But yeah, its totally an optional piece of canon (as everything else is)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:16:35-08:00","id":1056296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056293#post1056293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was going in with the assumption that 'you' were using the God-Machine and its attendent setting as written. But yeah, its totally an optional piece of canon (as everything else is)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, definitely. What I mean to say is, for a first time reader, the &quot;facts&quot; of the G-M can seem more concrete than they actually are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:19:11-08:00","id":1056297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056296#post1056296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, definitely. What I mean to say is, for a first time reader, the &quot;facts&quot; of the G-M can seem more concrete than they actually are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gotcha, but I'll refrain from saying more to avoid spoiling it for Ekorren.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:15:50-08:00","id":1056366,"title":"","content":"Combat is somewhat weird relative to the rest of the system. It's designed to have much smaller dicepools than other kinds of tasks and require you to spend willpower more often. Seven defense is pretty high though, much higher than most mortals will have. If your buddy couldn't fight a guard either the ST gave the guard too high stats or your friend didn't spec at all for combat and didn't know you can spend vitae to boost your traits as a vamp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T04:01:27-08:00","id":1056563,"title":"","content":"I will read more when I get home from work today but I've been wondering about something and thought this lunch break is a good time to ask.<br /> <br /> So I understand that I'm reading the revised rulebook (a.k.a. 2nd Edition). I understand that some (but not all) supplements have been revised as well, with Hunter: The Vigil as the next one coming. I've been googling a little but I can't seem to find a concrete list of which book is 2E, which is 1E, which is going to be revised and which is not going to be revised. For example, Mummy is a fairly new book, right, but was it written with the revisions in mind or was it written before then?<br /> <br /> We have revised books for Vampire, Werewolf, Mage and Geist right? Are there more? If I want to only buy 2E books, which ones should I get?<br /> <br /> After I've read Hurt Locker, what do you want me to tackle next? Dark Eras is interesting, but I feel like I should go for a splat first. Maybe Vampire since it feels like a must have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:31:35-08:00","id":1056582,"title":"","content":"Promethean is 2e, Geist is still upcoming. Demon and Beast have no first edition, they were made for 2e. I'd vote for doing Promethean next, but all six second editions are excellent. See how you feel about the God-Machine once you get there. If it intrigues you, Demon would be the one t do next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-01-2017, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:46:45-08:00","id":1056591,"title":"","content":"To be precise...<br /> <br /> Books in 2E rulesets:<ul><li><b>CoD Rulebook</b> ( optional, but good corebook )</li> <li><b>Hurt Locker</b> ( general supplement about violance to all CoD 2E )</li> <li><b>Vampire: The Requiem</b></li> <li><b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b></li> <li><b>Mage: The Awakening</b></li> <li><b>Promethean: The Created</b></li> <li><b>Beast: The Primodrial</b></li> </ul>Having mix of 1E and 2E:<ul><li><b>Demon: the Descent</b> ( it's using 2E rules but <b>do not</b> have rules in itself )</li> <li><b>Dark Eras </b>( rules version depends if 2E corebook is <i>now</i> )</li> </ul>Books now written for 2E:<ul><li><b>Changeling: The Lost</b></li> <li><b>Hunter: The Vigil</b></li> <li><b>Geist: The Sin-Eaters</b></li> </ul>Books in only 1E and <b>not</b> having planned ( for now ) update to 2E:<ul><li><b>Mummy: The Curse</b></li> <li><b>WoD: Inferno</b></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:55:54-08:00","id":1056594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056582#post1056582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean is 2e, Geist is still upcoming. Demon and Beast have no first edition, they were made for 2e. I'd vote for doing Promethean next, but all six second editions are excellent. See how you feel about the God-Machine once you get there. If it intrigues you, Demon would be the one t do next.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is it about Promethean that makes it the number one pick?<br /> <br /> I'm a little skeptical since I've been thinking about making the first splat one that I can easily stamp onto an existing mortal character. My understanding of Prometheans is that they don't work like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T06:10:42-08:00","id":1056599,"title":"","content":"You're correct about Prometheans not working like that. They start as supers and the end goal is to become a human. I'd recommend Vampire out of the splats that start human. It has the easiest/simplest rules and least complicated setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T06:11:46-08:00","id":1056600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056594#post1056594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little skeptical since I've been thinking about making the first splat one that I can easily stamp onto an existing mortal character. My understanding of Prometheans is that they don't work like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can use mortals-to-Prometheans transformation - you just need to kill human first. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Promethean player in my Mage game has character that was Created by mortal demiugre wanting to 'exchange souls' with body of freshly kill collage rugby jock. Now they are both dead and result Promethean is constantly wondering if he is more old alchemist, young jock or his own thing, because he has flashes of <i>both</i> alchemist and jocks memories. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T06:17:35-08:00","id":1056605,"title":"","content":"But that kinda skirts the fact that Prometheans are supposed to be completely new characters, and experimenting with the format isn't really what I'd suggest during a first read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:58:52-08:00","id":1056636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056591#post1056591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be precise...<br /> <br /> Books in 2E rulesets:<ul><li><b>CoD Rulebook</b> ( optional, but good corebook )</li> <li><b>Hurt Locker</b> ( general supplement about violance to all CoD 2E )</li> <li><b>Vampire: The Requiem</b></li> <li><b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b></li> <li><b>Mage: The Awakening</b></li> <li><b>Promethean: The Created</b></li> <li><b>Beast: The Primodrial</b></li> </ul>]</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Pack, and Secrets of the Covenants, Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes, and all the Demon supplements. Mortal Remains, though it's more of a conversion with additional unique material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-01-2017, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:58:57-08:00","id":1056637,"title":"","content":"Vampire is a solid pick for first splat. It's the original, and as such has the most polish to its themes and mechanics. Mage and Werewolf would also work for what you want, but I don't find their mechanics as easy to understand. Beast is another game that you can easily transition to from mortals, and their powers are mostly pretty straightforward, but the crossover focus makes it a somewhat weaker as a standalone game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:17:15-08:00","id":1056641,"title":"","content":"also, Changeling 2e is not out for a few months actually. It's just a lot of the drafts have been previewed for community testing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:21:54-08:00","id":1056643,"title":"","content":"Wyrd, I would not include Demon in the 1e/2e category, it is going to confuse people. Demon is straight 2e in terms of design and compatibility. It just came out before the God Machine Chronicles was called 2e. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056594#post1056594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it about Promethean that makes it the number one pick?<br /> <br /> I'm a little skeptical since I've been thinking about making the first splat one that I can easily stamp onto an existing mortal character. My understanding of Prometheans is that they don't work like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean was the game I was first introduced to and I think it captures both the beauty and horror of Chronicles of Darkness magnificently. Being a Promethean is simultaneously the shittiest thing to be in CofD and by far the most hopeful. It takes weird science and blends it seamlessly with classic horror and gothic fantasy.<br /> <br /> When you say &quot;stamping it on a preexisting character&quot; do you mean mechanically, or a mortal character becoming supernatural over the course of a story? If the latter, then yes, Promethean is not a good fit. If the former though, there is no reason you can take a character with the concept of mob flunkie, waitress, or hacker and apply the Promethean template to make a Promethean who was created to be a mob flunkie, waitress, or hacker. The only splat you can't do that for is Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:24:18-08:00","id":1056644,"title":"","content":"Throwing my vote in for Vampire as the first &quot;monster&quot; line, since the mechanics are relatively easy and clear and it stands very well as a one-monster-type game. Plus, the core doesn't carry as much setting &quot;baggage&quot; as the others, as it focuses on the mortal world and doesn't introduce too much more outside that. Although it should be noted that its 2e core wasn't <i>technically</i> a &quot;2e core&quot; when it first came out, so some of it may or may not seem a tiny bit messy or unclear to a newcomer... but aside from that, yeah, good first pick.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, Beast, and Promethean would be solid <i>second</i> pick-ups though, in all fairness. They're also mostly simple mechanically and are well-defined, but they each have their own issues. Werewolf adds a number of new creatures, leans hard on the Shadow and spirits, and the multiple forms for every PC could potentially be overwhelming to new players; Beast was explicitly designed with crossover in mind rather than just shrugging at the idea, so having at least one other monster type under your belt first could be a big help; and Promethean approaches things from the &quot;monster into human&quot; angle and requires <i>very</i> clear communication between the storyteller and players by virtue of the stories it wants to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 03-01-2017, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:43:35-08:00","id":1056710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>MISSING PERSONS: CHOOSE YOUR SETTING</b><br /> <br /> The methods where the Storyteller and the player design the game together doesn't appeal to me on either side of the table. When I'm Storyteller, I want to present the setting for my players. When I'm a player, I want to immerse myself in a world where I don't know what lurks around the corner. I blatantly ignore any suggestions in this chapter that doesn't fit my own playstyle---but I appreciate that it's there for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. It's really just a tool to use or not. Like, for the most part I create most of the setting and mysteries and surprises. Then I color my setting with inspiration from the created aspirations of the characters as well as the types of characters they created. So in that way they helped in the creation of the world they know very little about. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>EPHEMERAL BEINGS</b><br /> <br /> Another reference to the God-Machine. What does it mean when people begin to see its gears? Don't tell me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My lips are sealed ^.^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056183#post1056183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't tell me if I'm right, but you can tell me if I'm hot or cold.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My lips are sealed ^.^ but you're warm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:55:52-08:00","id":1056714,"title":"","content":"My Vote is For Demon:The Descent as your next read through for a few reasons:<br /> 1. It is by far my favorite book (love the splats, love the theses, love the antagonists, love the ST potential) and so would LOVE to see your thoughts as you read it.<br /> 2. You seem to be intrigued by The God-Machine. The Demon book might give you more to be intrigued about along those lines. <br /> 3. Other than humans, Demon seems to be the most companion to the Core 2nd edition book. I'm not fully certain but both seemed to be written with the other in mind. <br /> <br /> As for other considerations for your next read?<br /> - Vampire: The Requiem because it was the Flagship gameline and prolly the most simple to understand/readthrough themes wise<br /> - Mage: The Awakening because it takes the CofD setting and adds complexity. I find this the hardest to understand but that's kind of the appeal so if that is what intrigues you, choose Mage.<br /> - Changeling: The Lost because it is one of the bleakest of the CofD settings. I don't think it's quite out yet (the 2nd ed). Read this if you are looking to read one with a very different &quot;flair&quot; or atmosphere to it. <br /> - Hunter: The Vigil because it takes a lot of the human themes from the core and adds Hunters to the mix. It's like a continuation of a Human character sheet. If that is what you're looking for go with Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:09:54-08:00","id":1056722,"title":"","content":"I think this is a reasonably thorough list,<br /> <br /> <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b><ul><li>The God-Machine Chronicle</li> <li>Hurt Locker</li> <li>The Crossover Chronicle (Upcoming)</li> </ul><b>Vampire: the Requiem, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b> (Also known as Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle)<ul><li>Reap the Whirlwind</li> <li>Secrets of the Covenants</li> <li>A Thousand Years of Night (Upcoming)</li> <li>Half-Damned (Upcoming)</li> <li>Requiem for Regina (Dark Era, Elizabethan England)</li> <li>Unnamed Europe\u2019s Black Death Dark Era (Upcoming)</li> </ul><b>Werewolf: the Forsaken, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b><ul><li>The Pack</li> <li>The Bowery Dogs (Dark Era, 1970 New York City)</li> <li>Sundered World (Dark Era, Neolithic Period)</li> <li>The Wolf and the Raven (Dark Era, Viking Age)</li> <li>Forsaken by Rome (Upcoming Dark Era, 1<sup>st</sup> Century Rome)</li> </ul><b>Mage: the Awakening, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b><ul><li>Signs of Sorcery (upcoming)</li> <li>To the Strongest (Dark Era, Alexandrian India)</li> <li>Sundered World (Dark Era, Neolithic Period)</li> </ul><b>Promethean: the Created, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b><br /> <br /> <b>Changeling: the Lost, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b> (Upcoming, but a lot of material is available for free for open playtest)<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter: the Vigil, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b> (Upcomig)<ul><li>Mortal Remains (Technically a supplement for HtV 1<sup>st</sup> edition, but includes advice for updating HtV\u2019s core rules to 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition\u2019s system)</li> </ul><b>Geist: the Sin-Eaters, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition </b>(Upcoming)<br /> <br /> <b>Demon: the Descent</b><ul><li>Demon: the Descent Quickstart</li> <li>Flowers of Hell: the Demon Player\u2019s Guide</li> <li>Heirs to Hell</li> <li>Splintered City: Seattle</li> <li>The Demon Seed Collection</li> <li>Demon: Interface</li> <li>Demon Translation Guide</li> <li>Demon Storyteller\u2019s Guide</li> <li>Into the Cold (Dark Era, Cold War Germany)</li> <li>After the Fall (Dark Era, Ottoman conquest of Constantinople)</li> <li>Unnamed Russian Revolution Dark Era (upcoming)</li> </ul><b>Beast: the Primordial</b><ul><li>Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes</li> </ul><b>Deviant: the Renegates</b> (upcoming)<br /> <br /> <br /> I would recommend going for either Vampire as your first monster book (because it is mechanically the simplest), or, if you like what you see of the God-Machine when you get there, Demon (because it ties into the God-Machine stuff and has by far the most supplement support right now.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-01-2017, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:25:25-08:00","id":1056726,"title":"","content":"On the note of Demon: Strictly speaking, making Mortals into Demons is impossible. However, your players <i>can</i> take their characters into a Demon game because of *Spoilers*. They have to be okay with this, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:28:16-08:00","id":1056730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056563#post1056563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Vampire since it feels like a must have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I endorse this. <b>Requiem </b>2nd is a beautiful, stylish, noir-horror <i>book </i>just in its own right, and as an RPG it's probably got the easiest buy-in of the <b>Chronicles of Darkness </b>games, apart from maybe <b>Hunter</b>. Its social dynamics are simple but easy to complicate, and its powers are cool and evocative.<br /> <br /> That being said...<b>Demon: The Descent</b> is pretty close to what I'd consider a perfect roleplaying game, though you do have to like techgnostic espionage. It's not my favourite (it's tied with <b>Mage </b>for second), but you'd be hard pressed to find a game that better integrates mechanics and narrative and sheer coolness. It practically ran itself when I did a chronicle for it. It also has some of the best supplements that've come out for the Second Edition / CofD line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:13:24-08:00","id":1056758,"title":"","content":"I think you should read the books in the order in which they were released - Requiem, Forsaken, Awakening, Created, Lost, Vigil, Geist, Mummy, Demon.<br /> <br /> If you JUST want 2e, then I recommend Requiem, Forsaken, Awakening, Created, Demon. <br /> <br /> My Totally 100% Subjective Reasoning -<br /> <br /> Requiem is easily the easiest transition from mortals into the supernatural world. All Kindred were once mortal - it is, in fact, what makes them <i>Kindred. </i>Your mortal PCs could easily become Vampires, and even if you decide to start with them as Vampires, all of them were once mortal. The Five Covenants, or Factions, are all more or less tied to easy-to-understand themes. Power and Establishment, Revolution, Witchcraft and Balancing Humanity and the Beast, God and Faith, and Transhumanism. Super duper easy, and make great plots. Ghosts, Spirits, and Angels of the God-Machine are not tied to the setting at all, and can be used at your leisure or not at all. It's just Vampires, People, and lots and lots of Blood.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is a little weirder - though the players &quot;start&quot; human, Werewolves were never truly human at all and were born to experience their First Change. Werewolf is a really, really fun and immersive introduction to the Shadow/Spirit World, which focuses heavily on the Shadow and will get you understanding how it works and its taboos.<br /> <br /> Mage takes all that stuff up to 11. It has ALL of the complicated stuff, an expansive cosmology and dimensional map, and is effectively limited by your imagination. Your Mary Sue player will <i>love </i>it, if you're willing to put yourself through that. The only thing that makes Mages a LITTLE easy is that they are still technically human, just enlightened humans.<br /> <br /> Created is incredibly complicated - the characters were never human and are made (pretty much literally) from scratch. That can be super fun. There's also a Refinement dedicated to hanging out with all the other splats, so a working knowledge of other splats can help with that.<br /> <br /> I haven't played or read Demon, so I can't recommend or reject it. Everything I've heard about it is good stuff, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:20:20-08:00","id":1056763,"title":"","content":"Wow. Thanks for all the feedback. I'm leaning towards Vampire but I'm not going to make a decision until after I'm done with the book. I'm not sure if I'm intrigued with the God-Machine or intriduged with the idea that I don't know what it is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>GAME SYSTEMS</b><br /> <br /> The State of Twilight explains how ephemeral beings can exist in the real world while being incorporeal. You cannot attack a being in this state without some kind of \u201cspecial attack\u201d that explicitly allows it---I'm picturing the salt shotguns from Supernatural.<br /> <br /> These entities exist on a ten-scale rank which is actually a five-scale rank because only plot devices are above rank five. The Rank Table describes Rank, Trait Limits, Attribute Dots, Maximum Essence and Numina. To forcibly bind an ephemera, you subtract their Rank in dice from the attempt to bind them. The Trait Limits are the total number of dots you can distribute in their Skills and the Attribute Dots are what you distribute in their Attributes? So a Rank 1 ghost have five dots of Skills and 5-8 dots of Attributes? But this also determines the maximum traits, right? So a Rank 1 ghost can only have Strength 1 and Brawl 1, and these five dots must be distributed separately since they cannot be higher than one?<br /> <br /> There's a pragraph about <b>Supernatural Tolerance </b>describing the version of Rank associated with other supernatural creatures. I'm sure the various books describe this in better detail, but it says that some bonus is added to Resistance Attributes when contesting supernatural powers. So your Vampire is a good at defending against other Vampire effects, but he's no better than a mortal to defend against a firearm or a kick in the nuts? I imagine that they have their own cool traits to deal with that, but this particular \u201cpower level\u201d doesn't help in that regard.<br /> <br /> As someone used to Exalted, I'm used to Essence being some kind of mana pool used to fuel your superpowers. This is more like a secondary set of Willpower. Can an ephemeral being use both Essence and Willpower to boost the same action?<br /> <br /> Apparently human activity both feeds the Shadow Realm and pushes it away and the game won't tell me why. Intriguing. Is there an actual answer to this or is it up to Storyteller interpretation?<br /> <br /> Locus is a new word that is like a mix of a \u201clocation\u201d and a \u201cfocus.\u201d That's how I will remember it.<br /> <br /> My question above may be answered here. Ghosts usually use the average rating in each category from when they were alive---a person with Strength 3, Intelligence 3, and Presence 2 would become a ghost with Power 2. The others being Finesse and Resistance. Unlike what I assume previously, they don't have Skills at all. So they mostly roll Power/Finesse/Resistance + Rank? But then what was that deal about Trait Limits and Attribute Dots? And wasn't a Rank 1 ephemeral limited to one dot? Did I misunderstand all that?<br /> <br /> Ghosts have their Virtue and Vice, but their effects are reversed. There is a Fate optional rule I haven't read yet. Ghosts also have their Integrity. Spirits don't have Integrity, Virtue or Vice. They have Fates though, whatever that is. Angels lack Integrity but have Virtue and Vice.<br /> <br /> It's pretty cool that everyone understands angels as if they were speaking their native tongue \u2026 because they do.<br /> <br /> I like the <b>Bans</b>. They are creative ways to add some characteristics to the creatures. It can also be a story thread for the PCs to figure out what these Bans are. Same with <b>Banes</b>.<br /> <br /> Did I miss where they described what Numina was? I see the word all over but I dunno what it is.<br /> <br /> So we have Rank, Essence and Influence, where Rank determines the general power level of the being, Essence determines how much it can act before being drained, and Influence determines at what scope it can act. I kind of feel like I've completely misinterpreted how Rank affects the traits, but I'll probably figure it out by looking at some example antagonists. Hopefully there are a few listed.<br /> <br /> Are Numina and Manifestation Effects the same thing? I still don't get what Numina is. I checked the Lexicon and it wasn't there. Then I noticed that there was a part of this chapter dedicated to it and I kind of caught a glimpse of it and noticed that it reminded me of Conditions.<br /> <br /> If you wonder why I've never commented on the Gauntlet thing it's because I still don't really understand what it is and why it's named after an armored glove, but I feel stupid for not having figured it out yet. Maybe this is a good place to mention that English is my second language and that I'm always reading this after nine hours of work. I blame that for missing things.<br /> <br /> I was also distracted for more than an hour by Skype which made me realize that I should probably go back to this chapter and read this stuff again later. There are a lot of parts I'm going to read again later. The details about Anchors, Aspirations, and even combat, is starting to lose detail as I'm reading the book fairly slowly and from start to finish. When I'm done with the initial read through, I'm going to make a test character, test the rules in some simulated situations to \u201clearn by doing,\u201d and then I'm going to head straight into Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> Okay, that's a <b>Spirit Flowchart</b>. It's pretty, but I'm too tired to decipher it at the moment. Hmm, the Spirit of Uncle Tim's Vespa is a powerful entity indeed, and it wants to kill Uncle Tim in the real world. It has a decent Rank, a good amount of Essence and enough Influence to make some dramatic changes to the vespa and its surroundings. It already has an Influence Condition (Anchor) on the vespa, which allows it to add the Condition (Open) after having spent (Rank) scenes lusting over the vespa. This is then needed for the Manifestation Effect (Possess) which costs 3 Essence. Now it actually IS the vespa and it's trying to run Uncle Tim off a bridge. Uncle Tim's best bet of defeating the spirit is to actually destroy the vespa. If he does, it's a good breaking point. He loves that vespa.<br /> <br /> Hey! Numina are discrete magical powers! I learned something!<br /> <br /> <br /> Next time I'm reading <b>Mortal Interaction</b>. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:37:41-08:00","id":1056776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a pragraph about <b>Supernatural Tolerance </b>describing the version of Rank associated with other supernatural creatures. I'm sure the various books describe this in better detail, but it says that some bonus is added to Resistance Attributes when contesting supernatural powers. So your Vampire is a good at defending against other Vampire effects, but he's no better than a mortal to defend against a firearm or a kick in the nuts? I imagine that they have their own cool traits to deal with that, but this particular \u201cpower level\u201d doesn't help in that regard.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Supernatural Tolerance only applies to supernatural powers, and even then, not uniformly (it doesn't penalise Awakened magic in <b>Mage</b>, for instance, but that's a long story). And yes, they generally have more specific powers to deal with gunshots and nut kicking: Vampires have <i>Resilience</i>; werewolves have <i>you've made a poor life choice</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:42:26-08:00","id":1056779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>GAME SYSTEMS</b><br /> <br /> The State of Twilight explains how ephemeral beings can exist in the real world while being incorporeal. You cannot attack a being in this state without some kind of \u201cspecial attack\u201d that explicitly allows it---I'm picturing the salt shotguns from Supernatural.<br /> <br /> These entities exist on a ten-scale rank which is actually a five-scale rank because only plot devices are above rank five. The Rank Table describes Rank, Trait Limits, Attribute Dots, Maximum Essence and Numina. To forcibly bind an ephemera, you subtract their Rank in dice from the attempt to bind them. The Trait Limits are the total number of dots you can distribute in their Skills and the Attribute Dots are what you distribute in their Attributes? So a Rank 1 ghost have five dots of Skills and 5-8 dots of Attributes? But this also determines the maximum traits, right? So a Rank 1 ghost can only have Strength 1 and Brawl 1, and these five dots must be distributed separately since they cannot be higher than one?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I haven't read any further, so I have a hunch you answered your own question, but here's an extra example. For rank 1, you have between 5 and 8 dots of attributes to assign to the 3 attributes of power, finesse, and resistance. The limit for rank 1 spirits is 5 dots. If I wanted to make a Rank 1 spirit of a wildfire, I think this will be a pretty blunt creature. So I assign 5 dots in Power, 1 into Finesse and 1 into Resistance. If I wanted to make a Rank 2 spirit of a wildfire, I'm going to make it every bit as blunt and pour the maximum number of dots into power again. For Rank 2 that's 7. Since I have a total of 9-14 dots to spend, that leaves me with 2-7 left to spend. I'm going to put 3 into Resistance, since forest fires are hard to fight, and leave 1 in Finesse since there is nothing subtle about everything burning to the ground. So my Rank 2 spirit has Power 7, Finesse 1, and Resistance 3.<br /> <br /> Does that example help at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056776#post1056776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Supernatural Tolerance only applies to supernatural powers, and even then, not uniformly (it doesn't penalise Awakened magic in <b>Mage</b>, for instance, but that's a long story). And yes, they generally have more specific powers to deal with gunshots and nut kicking: Vampires have <i>Resilience</i>; werewolves have <i>you've made a poor life choice</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This quote is getting its own thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-01-2017, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T15:25:03-08:00","id":1056819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These entities exist on a ten-scale rank which is actually a five-scale rank because only plot devices are above rank five. The Rank Table describes Rank, Trait Limits, Attribute Dots, Maximum Essence and Numina. To forcibly bind an ephemera, you subtract their Rank in dice from the attempt to bind them. The Trait Limits are the total number of dots you can distribute in their Skills and the Attribute Dots are what you distribute in their Attributes? So a Rank 1 ghost have five dots of Skills and 5-8 dots of Attributes? But this also determines the maximum traits, right? So a Rank 1 ghost can only have Strength 1 and Brawl 1, and these five dots must be distributed separately since they cannot be higher than one?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question above may be answered here. Ghosts usually use the average rating in each category from when they were alive---a person with Strength 3, Intelligence 3, and Presence 2 would become a ghost with Power 2. The others being Finesse and Resistance. Unlike what I assume previously, they don't have Skills at all. So they mostly roll Power/Finesse/Resistance + Rank? But then what was that deal about Trait Limits and Attribute Dots? And wasn't a Rank 1 ephemeral limited to one dot? Did I misunderstand all that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank determines the maximum value for an ephemeral entity's traits (its Trait Limits), but the maximum is not equal to Rank. So, a Rank 1 ghost has 5-8 dots of Attributes that can be distributed between Power, Finesse, and Resistance, but none of those Attributes can go above 5. A Rank 2 ghost has 9-14 dots to distribute between its attributes, but none can be above a 7.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone used to Exalted, I'm used to Essence being some kind of mana pool used to fuel your superpowers. This is more like a secondary set of Willpower. Can an ephemeral being use both Essence and Willpower to boost the same action?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss where they described what Numina was? I see the word all over but I dunno what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Numina and Manifestation Effects the same thing? I still don't get what Numina is. I checked the Lexicon and it wasn't there. Then I noticed that there was a part of this chapter dedicated to it and I kind of caught a glimpse of it and noticed that it reminded me of Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Numen is a supernatural power an ephermeral entity has, such as being able to blast you with psychic energy or make nearby electronics go haywire. Numina is just the plural form of Numen. Manifestations are similar to Numina, in that they are supernatural abilities unique to ephemeral entities, but Manifestations specifically are what allow ephemeral entities to exist in the material world. Twilight form, for example, is a Manifestation - a state of being in which the entity is present in the material world, but invisible and incorporeal. Image is another Manifestation, in which the entity is incorporeal but visible. Materialize is a Manifestation in which the entity is fully corporeal and visible. Powers that allow an entity to take control of physical beings or objects, such as posession are also considered Manifestations. Essence does act kind of like a mana pool, which ephemeral entities spend to fuel their Numina and Manifestations, though it can also be spent to boost dice pools, much like Willpower. An entity can spend Essence and Willpower to boost the same roll if they choose to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently human activity both feeds the Shadow Realm and pushes it away and the game won't tell me why. Intriguing. Is there an actual answer to this or is it up to Storyteller interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wonder why I've never commented on the Gauntlet thing it's because I still don't really understand what it is and why it's named after an armored glove, but I feel stupid for not having figured it out yet. Maybe this is a good place to mention that English is my second language and that I'm always reading this after nine hours of work. I blame that for missing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would never have guessed that English was a second language for you, you use it very well. Anyway, the Gauntlet is a barrier between the material world and the spirit world. It gets its name not from the armored glove, but for a different meaning of the word, which essentially means a dangerous trial or an ordeal, particularly as something which has to be passed through. So, the reason that human activity pushes spirit activity away is because it strengthens the barrier between our world and the spirit world. The meta-narrative reason for this is that it's common in folklore for the untamed wilderness to be presented as being closer to the world of spirits/fairies/magic/etc, that &quot;the veil is thinner&quot; in the natural world than it is in the civilized world. In-setting, there isn't a real reason given for why exactly human activity strengthens the Gauntlet, it's mostly up to the storyteller. There are some possibilities hinted at in the Neolithic Dark Era, <i>Sundered World</i>, but they won't make much sense without background knowledge of werewolf. As for why human activity also strengthens spirit activity at the same time as it pushes the spirit world away, that's because humans are an abundant source of Resonance, which for spirits means an abundant source of Essence. We are strong abstract thinkers, and connect disparate concepts through symbolism very easily. Spirits thrive on symbolism, and are limited in what sort of Essence they can safely consume by conceptual links. Since humans are great at forming conceptual links, it's natural for spirits to want to be around humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Locus is a new word that is like a mix of a \u201clocation\u201d and a \u201cfocus.\u201d That's how I will remember it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's an existing English word. Chronicles of Darkness almost never makes up new words, but it does employ a lot of obscure English vocabulary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056763#post1056763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that's a <b>Spirit Flowchart</b>. It's pretty, but I'm too tired to decipher it at the moment. Hmm, the Spirit of Uncle Tim's Vespa is a powerful entity indeed, and it wants to kill Uncle Tim in the real world. It has a decent Rank, a good amount of Essence and enough Influence to make some dramatic changes to the vespa and its surroundings. It already has an Influence Condition (Anchor) on the vespa, which allows it to add the Condition (Open) after having spent (Rank) scenes lusting over the vespa. This is then needed for the Manifestation Effect (Possess) which costs 3 Essence. Now it actually IS the vespa and it's trying to run Uncle Tim off a bridge. Uncle Tim's best bet of defeating the spirit is to actually destroy the vespa. If he does, it's a good breaking point. He loves that vespa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seem's like you've pretty well deciphered the flowchart, which is no small feat - it's pretty dense. One thing I would note is that only ghosts build off of the Anchor Condition (and ghosts only build off of Anchor). Spirits only build off of Resonant, and Angels only build off of Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-01-2017, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T15:48:32-08:00","id":1056823,"title":"","content":"Locus is older than that. It's a latin word meaning location, and while it is used English it's mainly in specialized fields so it's not surprising people aren't familiar with it. It's also a common etymological root for many words, such as 'location' in English or 'lokal' in our native Swedish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-01-2017, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T07:30:42-08:00","id":1057589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1056722#post1056722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a reasonably thorough list,<br /> <br /> <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b><ul><li>The God-Machine Chronicle</li> <li>Hurt Locker</li> <li>The Crossover Chronicle (Upcoming)</li> </ul><b>Vampire: the Requiem, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b> (Also known as Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle)<ul><li>Reap the Whirlwind</li> <li>Secrets of the Covenants</li> <li>A Thousand Years of Night (Upcoming)</li> <li>Half-Damned (Upcoming)</li> <li>Requiem for Regina (Dark Era, Elizabethan England)</li> <li>Unnamed Europe\u2019s Black Death Dark Era (Upcoming)</li> </ul><b>Werewolf: the Forsaken, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b><ul><li>The Pack</li> <li>The Bowery Dogs (Dark Era, 1970 New York City)</li> <li>Sundered World (Dark Era, Neolithic Period)</li> <li>The Wolf and the Raven (Dark Era, Viking Age)</li> <li>Forsaken by Rome (Upcoming Dark Era, 1<sup>st</sup> Century Rome)</li> </ul><b>Mage: the Awakening, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b><ul><li>Signs of Sorcery (upcoming)</li> <li>To the Strongest (Dark Era, Alexandrian India)</li> <li>Sundered World (Dark Era, Neolithic Period)</li> </ul><b>Promethean: the Created, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b><br /> <br /> <b>Changeling: the Lost, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b> (Upcoming, but a lot of material is available for free for open playtest)<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter: the Vigil, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</b> (Upcomig)<ul><li>Mortal Remains (Technically a supplement for HtV 1<sup>st</sup> edition, but includes advice for updating HtV\u2019s core rules to 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition\u2019s system)</li> </ul><b>Geist: the Sin-Eaters, 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition </b>(Upcoming)<br /> <br /> <b>Demon: the Descent</b><ul><li>Demon: the Descent Quickstart</li> <li>Flowers of Hell: the Demon Player\u2019s Guide</li> <li>Heirs to Hell</li> <li>Splintered City: Seattle</li> <li>The Demon Seed Collection</li> <li>Demon: Interface</li> <li>Demon Translation Guide</li> <li>Demon Storyteller\u2019s Guide</li> <li>Into the Cold (Dark Era, Cold War Germany)</li> <li>After the Fall (Dark Era, Ottoman conquest of Constantinople)</li> <li>Unnamed Russian Revolution Dark Era (upcoming)</li> </ul><b>Beast: the Primordial</b><ul><li>Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes</li> </ul><b>Deviant: the Renegates</b> (upcoming)<br /> <br /> <br /> I would recommend going for either Vampire as your first monster book (because it is mechanically the simplest), or, if you like what you see of the God-Machine when you get there, Demon (because it ties into the God-Machine stuff and has by far the most supplement support right now.)</div> </div> </div> </div>One addition to this list. Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies is technically a 1e book, but it was written with the then forthcoming Blood &amp; Smoke (which is now Vampire 2e) in mind. It was written by Ben Baugh, David Brookshaw, David Hill, and Travis Stout. Those last three names are the Lead Developers of Mage 2e/Deviant: The Renegade, Changeling 2e/Hurt Locker, and Geist 2e respectively. It's about as awesome as you would expect coming from them. <br /> <br /> If you do go the Vampire route, I'd suggest reading Vampire 2e, Blood Sorceries, then Secrets of the Covenants in that order. The Blood Sorceries mechanics are present in Secrets of the Covenants, although you don't need the former to use that latter, and it was done in a way that there's not really any lost word count if you aren't using Blood Sorceries. I can't say more without wandering into spoilers, but it's a very cool system and one of my favourites, having been based off Mage's magic style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-03-2017, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T08:19:28-08:00","id":1057601,"title":"","content":"<b>MORTAL INTERACTION</b><br /> <br /> The number of successes required to learn the ban/bane of an ephemeral entity through research is a good suggestion to help STs along. I'll probably use it as written sometimes and combine it with some story requirements for rare antagonists with some more power.<br /> <br /> Is the roll mentioned in <b>Contact </b>the same as the one in <b>Research</b>, or should it vary depending on the situation? I imagine that you talking to a haunted house would maybe use Presence or Manipulation instead of Intelligence.<br /> <br /> <i>Esoteric Armory </i>is a cool Merit.<br /> <br /> Not much to say about Summonings, Exorcisms, Abjurations, Wardings and Bindings. Can everyone pull this off (especially abjurations) or is the action limited to specific individuals? It doesn't really say. It only explains how the action is done.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>HORRORS</b><br /> <br /> Oh, time to create something nasty. Let's start with a concept. I want to create a <i>Peeper</i>! A fairly weak and slender creature that enjoys looking at people through keyholes and windows. It's Aspirations is to \u201clook at people without being seen, to see who they truly are.\u201d<br /> <br /> I feel like the Peeper should be a Potency 2 creature. It's more frightening than deadly.<br /> <br /> I'm going to give my Peeper the Virtue (Curious) and the Vice (Silent).<br /> <br /> It doesn't say whether or not Attributes start with a dot so I'm going to assume that they don't.<br /> <br /> <b>Intelligence:</b> 2; <b>Wits:</b> 3; <b>Resolve:</b> 2.<br /> <b>Strength:</b> 1; <b>Dexterity:</b> 5; <b>Stamina:</b> 1.<br /> <b>Presence:</b> 2; <b>Manipulation:</b> 2; <b>Composure:</b> 4.<br /> <br /> The Peeper stands there to watch you, and it's very quick to get away if you catch it in your periphery.<br /> <br /> I'm supposed to select three Dread Powers now for my Peeper. Let's skip right to them and see what we've got. <i>Eye Spy</i> helps the Peeper to peep, so that's a given. I also think <i>Jump Scare</i> and <i>Madness and Terror</i> are fitting. The Peeper can use various tools to help him peep.<br /> <br /> <b>Athletics:</b> 4; <b>Brawl:</b> 1; <b>Larceny:</b> 2; <b>Stealth:</b> 4; <b>Intimidation:</b> 2; <b>Subterfuge:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>Fast Reflexes:</b> 3; <b>Patient:</b> 1; <b>Fleet of Foot:</b> 3<br /> <br /> Should you catch its peeping gaze, it'd scare you so much you shit yourself. Then it runs away, agile like the little dick it is, so that it can peep on you again another day. It's behind you! Taka-taka-taka-taka! It ran away. That's the sound of it running away. Now it's behind you again! <i>Boo!</i><br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8; <b>Size: </b>4; <b>Speed: </b>17 (Strength + Dexterity + 8 [Creature type] + 3 [Merit]); <b>Health: </b>5; <b>Initiative Modifier: </b>+9; <b>Defense: </b>7<br /> <br /> The Peeper is afraid of mirrors. If it catches a glimpse of itself, it will be affected by its own Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> How's that for a first horror?<br /> <br /> <br /> Later today I will start reading the <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T08:24:23-08:00","id":1057603,"title":"","content":"The Clanbooks are also specifically called out as being (mostly) useable in Vampire 2e. The mechanics aren't perfectly matched up, and a few fluff points have changed, with the change in Ventrue and Predator's Taint especially, but overall they're still fantastic reads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T08:24:42-08:00","id":1057604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057601#post1057601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>MORTAL INTERACTION</b><br /> How's that for a first horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm stealing it! The Horror rules are one of my favourite parts of CofD, and they make the core book entirely worth it. Its so easy to create everything from a gremlin to Cthulhu to Monty Python's Rabbit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T09:25:56-08:00","id":1057625,"title":"","content":"Isn't one dot in an Attribute meant to model major deficiencies? Like, one dot in Strength would be a small child or someone with atrophied muscles. And one dot in Intelligence would be a person with an IQ below 50. I think that's why at least for characters, you start with one dot in each automatically. I haven't gotten the full 2e rulebook though, so could someone confirm this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T09:32:53-08:00","id":1057628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057625#post1057625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't one dot in an Attribute meant to model major deficiencies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fuck no. That's the domain of Conditions (or Flaws in 1e).<br /> <br /> One dot just represents below average, much like three dots represents above-average capabilities in that trait without being extraordinary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T09:33:09-08:00","id":1057630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057625#post1057625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't one dot in an Attribute meant to model major deficiencies? Like, one dot in Strength would be a small child or someone with atrophied muscles. And one dot in Intelligence would be a person with an IQ below 50. I think that's why at least for characters, you start with one dot in each automatically. I haven't gotten the full 2e rulebook though, so could someone confirm this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters do, Horrors &amp; Ephemerals do not as far as I am aware. In 1e, Pandorans could have 0 Int and Man, although that has changed in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T09:39:57-08:00","id":1057635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057625#post1057625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't one dot in an Attribute meant to model major deficiencies? Like, one dot in Strength would be a small child or someone with atrophied muscles. And one dot in Intelligence would be a person with an IQ below 50. I think that's why at least for characters, you start with one dot in each automatically. I haven't gotten the full 2e rulebook though, so could someone confirm this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not major deficiencies, just below-average ability in the Attribute in question. Strength 1 is like someone who never exercises. Intelligence 1 is like someone with IQ below 100 (100 being the average). Disabilities are modeled by Persistent Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T09:48:17-08:00","id":1057638,"title":"","content":"Huh. the more you know. So, does that mean three dots in anything puts in something like the top 10% of all beings for that ability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T10:21:21-08:00","id":1057645,"title":"","content":"Three dots is explicitly called 'above average.'<br /> <br /> Page 30, 'All characters start with one dot in each Attribute, which is below average for that Attribute. Two dots represents average ability, three dots is above average, and four dots is someone who is truly exceptional. A character with five dots in an Attribute has reached the peak of human potential within that ability.'<br /> <br /> Four dots sounds more like the top 10%, with five being top 1%. But there's no hard numbers so you could fidget with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T10:29:12-08:00","id":1057647,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so a dice pool of 3 represents succeeding about half the time in a stressful enough situation to require rolling. That means 2 in an Attribute and 1 in a Skill - or the other way around - is a &quot;normal&quot; dice pool for the Storytelling system. More than that, either in Attribute or Skill, means you're above average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T10:47:38-08:00","id":1057656,"title":"","content":"People are taught differently. When I first started playing NWoD back in 2008, I was explicitly told by my ST that 1s in an attribute represented extreme deficiency, and that I had to be 2 even if I wanted my character to be less than smart or never exercises, because a 1 meant I was disabled. Because of this, I always saw players who put a 1 in something because 'he never exercises' as being typical min-maxing power gamers trying to get higher stats in things they plan to use more. I still kind of get aneurysms when a player hands me a sheet with a 1 in an attribute.<br /> <br /> I'm getting better, because I am coming around to the idea that 1 just means you're bad at something. But I only let my players choose to have a 1 in something if they plan to roleplay that 1. If they just want to 'be able to do it but not great' then they gotta put at least 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T10:59:13-08:00","id":1057662,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry you had that experience but even then the book said otherwise.<br /> <br /> 1 dot was 'Poor. Unexercised, unpracticed or inept.' 2 was 'Average. The result of occasional effort or application.' 3 was 'Good. Regular practice or effort, or naturally talented. Four was 'Exceptional. Frequently applied, tested and honed, or naturally gifted.' And five was 'Outstanding. The peak of normal human capability. Continuously exercised or naturally blessed.'<br /> <br /> To be fair, a lot of people came into the game from old World of Darkness and it's possible they brought preconceptions over. But glancing at my 20th Anniversary Vampire book it still has 1 dot as 'Poor,' with 1 dot of Strength allowing for the lifting of 40 pounds which is poor, Strengthwise, but probably not considered 'extreme deficiency.' Perhaps it's a Dungeons and Dragons thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:12:51-08:00","id":1057664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057638#post1057638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. the more you know. So, does that mean three dots in anything puts in something like the top 10% of all beings for that ability?</div> </div> </div> </div> No, 1 is below average, 2 is average, 3 is above average, 4 is exceptional, 5 is world-class.<br /> <br /> To put it in D&amp;D Ability Score terms , 1 dot is 10-11, 2 dots is 12-13, 3 dots is 14-15, 4 dots is 16-17, 5 dots is 18.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:13:36-08:00","id":1057665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057662#post1057662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry you had that experience but even then the book said otherwise.<br /> <br /> 1 dot was 'Poor. Unexercised, unpracticed or inept.' 2 was 'Average. The result of occasional effort or application.' 3 was 'Good. Regular practice or effort, or naturally talented. Four was 'Exceptional. Frequently applied, tested and honed, or naturally gifted.' And five was 'Outstanding. The peak of normal human capability. Continuously exercised or naturally blessed.'<br /> <br /> To be fair, a lot of people came into the game from old World of Darkness and it's possible they brought preconceptions over. But glancing at my 20th Anniversary Vampire book it still has 1 dot as 'Poor,' with 1 dot of Strength allowing for the lifting of 40 pounds which is poor, Strengthwise, but probably not considered 'extreme deficiency.' Perhaps it's a Dungeons and Dragons thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was almost definitely D&amp;D preconceptions. But the Golden Rule says ST always wins, so really if your ST wants to make 1s into disabilities, then that's their prerogative. I still think of 1s as not necessarily disabilities, but the result of deficiency, just not the same. A person who never exercises would still be Strength 2, imo, as long as they occasionally go outside and walk around and pick up boxes and eat well. Someone with Strength 1, in my opinion, would have to be a shut-in, or elderly, or unhealthy in some way. They would have to play being a total weakling. But that's my call. It also makes more sense to me that a character might have 2s in all stats than a 1 in one physical stat and a 3 in another. (It's justifiable, and I'd accept it with good justification, but it's still weird to me.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:14:31-08:00","id":1057666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057664#post1057664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, 1 is below average, 2 is average, 3 is above average, 4 is exceptional, 5 is world-class.<br /> <br /> To put it in D&amp;D Ability Score terms , 1 dot is 10-11, 2 dots is 12-13, 3 dots is 14-15, 4 dots is 16-17, 5 dots is 18.</div> </div> </div> </div>10-11 is average in D&amp;D though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:17:01-08:00","id":1057667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057666#post1057666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10-11 is average in D&amp;D though.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but what D&amp;D considers below average gives you a penalty on related rolls, which a 1 in an Attribute does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:22:28-08:00","id":1057668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057665#post1057665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone with Strength 1, in my opinion, would have to be a shut-in, or elderly, or unhealthy in some way. They would have to play being a total weakling.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, if you're voluntarily playing a character with such a disadvantage in Chronicles of Darkness Second Edition, you should be getting a Beat when that disadvantage causes problems for yourself or the group. That's why they're represented by Persistent Conditions. If you don't have a Persistent Condition, then having one fewer die on tasks associated with that Attribute than someone with a 2 is sufficient to represent the difference between you in that Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-03-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:26:34-08:00","id":1057672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057667#post1057667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but what D&amp;D considers below average gives you a penalty on related rolls, which a 1 in an Attribute does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably what is average for a regular person is below average for someone like an adventurer but I'm not sure that mattered in their development.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057665#post1057665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Golden Rule says ST always wins, so really if your ST wants to make 1s into disabilities, then that's their prerogative.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may want to rethink this. The storyteller and players are playing the game together, and while the storyteller frames the setting, they are not the Authority and having a golden rule like this is not going to help a cooperative gaming experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-03-2017, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:26:42-08:00","id":1057673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057668#post1057668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, if you're voluntarily playing a character with such a disadvantage in Chronicles of Darkness Second Edition, you should be getting a Beat when that disadvantage causes problems for yourself or the group. That's why they're represented by Persistent Conditions. If you don't have a Persistent Condition, then having one fewer die on tasks associated with that Attribute than someone with a 2 is sufficient to represent the difference between you in that Attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I usually just tell them not to play a character with a 1 in an attribute if they don't want to be bad at something....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:29:33-08:00","id":1057676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057673#post1057673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually just tell them not to play a character with a 1 in an attribute if they don't want to be bad at something....</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is your prerogative as Storyteller, but it is contrary to 2e design philosophy. Disadvantages should grant Beats when they hinder the party. That's a core function of the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:32:20-08:00","id":1057677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057672#post1057672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arguably what is average for a regular person is below average for someone like an adventurer but I'm not sure that mattered in their development.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You may want to rethink this. The storyteller and players are playing the game together, and while the storyteller frames the setting, they are not the Authority and having a golden rule like this is not going to help a cooperative gaming experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. D&amp;D and Chronicles of Darkness are working from different definitions of &quot;average&quot;, and that's (part of) what causes this dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:33:24-08:00","id":1057678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057676#post1057676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is your prerogative as Storyteller, but it is contrary to 2e design philosophy. Disadvantages should grant Beats when they hinder the party. That's a core function of the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I still disagree because I don't think it's quite the same thing. I could be wrong. But I feel like conditions are the result of roleplaying, and events over the course of the game. Theoretically, someone could start with a condition if they wished, but I have yet to have that happen. Conditions - and gaining beats - encourages roleplaying. Choosing to get a 1 in attribute is either just an aspect of your character, or you really just wanted higher stats in attributes you planned to use more, which I do not encourage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:47:23-08:00","id":1057684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057656#post1057656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting better, because I am coming around to the idea that 1 just means you're bad at something. But I only let my players choose to have a 1 in something if they plan to roleplay that 1. If they just want to 'be able to do it but not great' then they gotta put at least 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure why it's more important for a player to commit to roleplaying a one-dot Attribute than, say, a three-dot Attribute. Or a two-dot. Or a four, which is perfectly feasible for a Vampire or Mage character who gets to distribute an extra starting dot. A one-dot Attribute has comparatively little actual in-game effect: it makes you worse at things, but no more worse than having three dots makes you better at it. If it were meant to represent a strong deficiency, it does a rather poor job of it. (It's not; Persistent Conditions represent that. That's why there are Conditions like Blind, Crippled, and Mute, not just to represent an edge case where your character might be driven Mute mid-game.)<br /> <br /> It also kind of messes up the distribution math. Starting dot spreads are tight in nWoD, probably with the choice of having to sink an Attribute to one dot to favor another baked in. Putting this kind of emphasis on one-dot Attributes effectively means every character's tertiary Attributes are always going to be 2/2/2, which while not broken is a rather bland boiling down of choice.<br /> <br /> Having one dot in an Attribute is its own drawback already; it doesn't need to be magnified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 03-03-2017, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:47:40-08:00","id":1057685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057678#post1057678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I still disagree because I don't think it's quite the same thing. I could be wrong. But I feel like conditions are the result of roleplaying, and events over the course of the game. Theoretically, someone could start with a condition if they wished, but I have yet to have that happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's explicitly possible to start with one or more Persistent Conditions. In fact, Persistent Conditions explicitly replace Flaws from 1st edition, which could only be taken at character creation and grant 1XP once per session when they hinder the character or the group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057678#post1057678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conditions - and gaining beats - encourages roleplaying. Choosing to get a 1 in attribute is either just an aspect of your character,</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that Conditions are a disadvantages that result from roleplay and that the disadvantage of having a 1 in an Attribute should be reflected in the roleplay. Why, then, is this particular expression of roleplaying a disadvantage an exception to the way you normally view Conditions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057678#post1057678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or you really just wanted higher stats in attributes you planned to use more, which I do not encourage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those things that seems to bother some GMs for reasons I have never understood. Should players not want higher stats in the Attributes they plan to use? Should they not be ok with having lower stats in the Attributes they don't plan to use? Is it not versimilar that people who regularly utilize their strength be stronger than those who use it only occasionally, and that those who rarely use their Strength be weaker than those who use it occasionally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-03-2017, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:59:58-08:00","id":1057693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057685#post1057685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is one of those things that seems to bother some GMs for reasons I have never understood. Should players not want higher stats in the Attributes they plan to use? Should they not be ok with having lower stats in the Attributes they don't plan to use? Is it not versimilar that people who regularly utilize their strength be stronger than those who use it only occasionally, and that those who rarely use their Strength be weaker than those who use it occasionally?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. You should be good at some stuff. You should be bad at some stuff. The worst characters tend to be jacks of all trades, masters of none.<br /> <br /> I guess if a player chose to game the system to the point that their character could one-shot vampires with his axe, but couldn't otherwise function as a human being, then it would be a problem, but even then, the basic character creation system makes it pretty hard to do that, and either A) that person doesn't have an adequate idea of the ST and other players' expectations, or B) they totally do, and they're actually more interested in the downsides than the killdozing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:05:43-08:00","id":1057695,"title":"","content":"For the record, I do require people to roleplay having a 3 in an attribute. I also require them to roleplay having a 4 in an attribute. And I certainly require them to roleplay having a 5 in an attribute. The only dot rating that I don't expect people to explictly roleplay having is 2, because 2 is average. There's nothing exceptional or detracting from having a 2. I expect someone with a 3 in Intelligence to be an intelligent character. I expect someone with a 4 in Intelligence to be an exceptionally intelligent character. 5 is a genius. I don't know where you got the idea that I only require different roleplaying for a 1 in an attribute, but everyone else doesn't have to live up to their dot rating.<br /> <br /> As for why it bothers me, it's mostly because every game I've ever been in with an Attribute 1 person has involved them basically playing their 1 Attribute person as being totally normal at that attribute, until it comes to rolls, while benefiting from having the higher trait all the time. It's always come across to me as cheating. I don't imagine it will ever stop being such. But, as noted, it's everyone's prerogative as ST to do what makes sense to them. I've never complained about those Attribute 1 people, just kind of grimaced and went on with my life.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:08:57-08:00","id":1057699,"title":"","content":"*cough* *cough*<br /> <br /> (points at quote in OP saying &quot;try not to digress too much&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:57:32-08:00","id":1057755,"title":"","content":"Let's talk about Peepers. Aren't they nasty little fuckers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T14:07:51-08:00","id":1057758,"title":"","content":"yep, but also hilarious. Speaking of Horrors, I think you'll like this thread here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...he-horror-show<br /> <br /> P</a>.S. Reighnell is pretty awesome. Show them your Peepers. I think they'll love them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T14:46:10-08:00","id":1057770,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ever since I started reading this book, I've been going on and on about how I don't know what the God-Machine is and I didn't want anyone to spoil it for me. Well, I have finally arrived.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>THE GOD MACHINE CHRONICLE</b></span><br /> <br /> The text begins with a question: <i>\u201cWhat is the God-Machine?\u201d</i> I feel my quest nearing its end. I feel like I'm about to unravel a truth that will forever change my life. I'm reading the next sentence: <i>\u201cThat question doesn't have a single, easy answer ...\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>FUUUUUUUUCKK!</b></i><br /> <br /> Seriously, though.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to decipher the art piece. There's some kind of floating obelisk with jellyfish tendrils and a creepy eye. Maybe my previous idea that the God-Machine is like if \u201cCthulhu's home dimension had sex with a grandfather clock\u201d is close to the truth after all. That picture feels Lovecraftian.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>VOICE OF AN ANGEL</b><br /> <br /> So the God-Machine created the world for the angels. These angels desired \u201chumans\u201d to serve them. First they took animals and tried to make them \u201chumans\u201d, but they ended up becoming violent demons instead. Having learned from that mistake, they managed to create their humans and spread them across the world. Humans didn't die, but instead went to sleep in the ground when they got old and were rejuvinated into youth. They created a city \u201cwhere the orbit of the moon crossed the orbit of the sun.\u201d I'm not going to try to learn what that means. Esoteric stuff.<br /> <br /> So after the humans in Eclipse Town got angry with their supernatural politicians, they whined to the God-Machine and got an answer in words. So the God-Machine can communicate with words? It is an actual sentient being then?<br /> <br /> The humans debated for seven years after they got their answer. That doesn't seem very human-like. Humans wouldn't debate for seven years. They would act on impulse and cause a bunch of chaos, and then try to debate first after they have ruined a bunch of things.<br /> <br /> Angels sleep apparently. And they have red blood (assuming the text refers to angel blood). But they are also ephemeral beings according to the Antagonist chapter. Can ephemeral beings sleep and have red blood? I guess. I just didn't expect it. Or maybe these \u201cAncient Ones\u201d are different from the angels in the Antagonist chapter. Maybe these are old super-angels while the other ones are mini-angels pooped out by the God-Machine on occasion. Apparently the survivors were called <i>Furies</i>. I suppose the Furies are basically arch-angels then?<br /> <br /> Ah, this is cool. The Furies named themselves after concepts and shaped the world (and mankind) through curses. This then nerfed humans into stupid mortals. I guess the pre-cursed humans were the kinds to debate for seven years and it was the post-cursed humans that went ahead and acted irresponsibly and built huge walls and created Snapchat. Well, the Torment Fury who created \u201cwyff-man\u201d and \u201cwo-man\u201d wasn't very cool. That was extremely silly.<br /> <br /> So there are four Furies who haven't cursed humans yet, but who are waiting to do so?<br /> <br /> Right, I had forgot that all of this was said to a 12 year old by an angel. Are we sure this whole God-Machine Chronicle isn't just the figment of a child's imagination?<br /> <br /> We go on to learn about how demon cults guard hidden chambers under the Sphinx of Egypt. One Fury is Australian because he was sure that Australia wouldn't be discovered by man for a long time. Apparently he only considered \u201cwhite man\u201d because there is evidence of Aboriginal people in Australia dating back as far as 60 000 years. Seems like this Fury didn't consider that. Maybe he took the name Racist. Oh wait, the text continues and says that Aboriginals actually were there and gazed upon him and could read dreams. So maybe he took the name Stupid instead. He should have picked Antarctica.<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, I actually think this is a fun and interesting genesis story. It's definitely not what I expected it to be.<br /> <br /> The other Furies built civilizations elsewhere. One bitter Fury noticed that some of these civilizations were close to mastering <i>Star Rites </i>that apparently turn humans into gods.<br /> <br /> Electromagnetic waves are the shadows of the voice of the God-Machine. I like the part about Hughes and his discovery of electromagnetic patterns. That's the kind of mystery story I enjoy and would enjoy roleplaying.<br /> <br /> Apparently Oppenheimer was a demon cultist. That's kind of silly, but it fits the theme of the setting so I'm okay with it. I did enjoy the story about the Apollo missions being a cover and austronauts bringing back the skeleton of Death.<br /> <br /> Okay, the intro text is over. I actually enjoyed this. It's a bit more sci-fi than I expected it to be, but I enjoy stories like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FICTION: DAVID NELSON</b><br /> <br /> Interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>GEARS WITHIN GEARS: THE GOD-MACHINE CHRONICLE</b></span><br /> <br /> \u201cPeople see something the God-Machine intends to keep secret---or they are singled out as the right <i>shape</i> of person for a particular task, the right size cog with the right number of teeth---and they disappear.\u201d<br /> <br /> I picture some Junji Ito horror show in my mind---the spiral of humans at the end of Uzumaki. There's been nothing to suggest that the God-Machine is made up of anything other than \u201csupernatural stuff\u201d but wouldn't it be creepy if parts of the God-Machine are actual human cogs?<br /> <br /> Okay, so it is an actual interdimensional machine. Is it built by something or is it the cause of its own existence? If it's interdimensional, and controls spacetime, then it wouldn't need a beginning or an end because it makes time meaningless. I'm going with the idea that the God-Machine is its own cause unless something in the book says otherwise.<br /> <br /> Now the book outright states that the truths about the God-Machine are undetermined. I'm okay with that.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine's structure consists of both literal and figurative parts. This is good, because it lets me bring something physical and substantial into my games if I want to. And it lets me be more esoteric when I want to.<br /> <br /> Now it says that the God-Machine can't violate the laws of physics. But earlier it suggested that it was interdimensional with tendrils stretching all over the multiverse. Maybe it has to abide to the laws of physics of the dimension it taps into, but it cannot alter the laws of any of those dimensions. At least not willingly.<br /> <br /> But can it do so unwillingly?<br /> <br /> The notes about <b>Infrastructure </b>and <b>Linchpins </b>were very inspiring. I can think of a few ways I can integrate that into my stories.<br /> <br /> The optional rule about <b>Fate</b> doesn't really seem necessary to me. I think Aspirations are enough. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T15:02:27-08:00","id":1057772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057770#post1057770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I picture some Junji Ito horror show in my mind---the spiral of humans at the end of Uzumaki. There's been nothing to suggest that the God-Machine is made up of anything other than \u201csupernatural stuff\u201d but wouldn't it be creepy if parts of the God-Machine are actual human cogs?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to enjoy the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> This half of the book is reprinted from a previous book, where the God-Machine Chronicle and a more basic form of the CofD 2e ruleset was presented as a non-standalone bolt-on for the 1e rulebook. I mention this only to note that a large swath of that book's content, mostly from the Introduction chapter which is analogous to the part you are reading now, was cut for space, and I think that's a shame, because the cut content was a very accessible walkthrough of a ground's-eye view of what the God-Machine is, why it is the way it is from a storytelling perspective, what its purposes in a game are, and how to execute it. I'm interested to see if the removal of that content will impact your ability to digest the material or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:31:03-08:00","id":1057819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057770#post1057770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now it says that the God-Machine can't violate the laws of physics. But earlier it suggested that it was interdimensional with tendrils stretching all over the multiverse. Maybe it has to abide to the laws of physics of the dimension it taps into, but it cannot alter the laws of any of those dimensions. At least not willingly.<br /> <br /> But can it do so unwillingly?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a Clarke's Third Law thing. It can't violate the laws of physics, but its understanding of the laws of physics are sufficiently advanced to the point where it can do things that might <i>look like</i> violating those laws to us primitive humans.<br /> <br /> So yeah, now that you're here, I'm going to give the meta-game answer to what the God-Machine Chronicle is, because it's been driving me crazy waiting this long. I'll put it in spoiler tags for now, in case you want to finish the section before reading this, but I can't wait any longer.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So, when Onyx Path decided to do a second edition of the game, which was called World of Darkness, or colloquially as &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness at the time (as opposed to Classic World of Darkness, which previously had the name World of Darkness), the owners of the IP (Crowd Control Publishing at the time) were not too keen on the idea of a new edition. D&amp;D's identity crisis and ensuing edition war was a still a recent memory, and new editions were probably seen as bad publicity. So instead, Onyx Path pitched the idea of &quot;Chronicle books&quot;, which would feature optional rules updates to 1st edition alongside a canned chronicle (which is CofD's term for a campaign, much as story is CofD's term for an adventure and chapter is it's term for a session). The God-Machine chronicle was the first of these chronicle books, and it is still available for sale. The next such book was Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, which was the equivalent of the God-Machine Chronicle for Vampire the Requiem. This book sold incredibly well, but caused a lot of confusion over these rules updates, and what they meant for &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness going forward. The financial success of Blood and Smoke was apparently enough to convince Crowd Control that it was safe to call the new edition what it was, and Blood and Smoke was re-released with a new title and cover, as Vampire the Requiem Second Edition. Since Onyx Path was finally allowed to officially call Second Edition what it was, they decided to publish a proper core rulebook for Second Edition, since the God-Machine Chronicle had been written as a set of patch notes and had to be used alongside the First Edition core book. Around the time that the book that you've been reading was in development under the name World of Darkness Second Edition, Paradox Interactive bought the World of Darkness and Classic World of Darkness intellectual properties from Crowd Control, and changed Classic World of Darkness' name back to just World of Darkness, and the &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness to Chronicles of Darkness. So, the book's name was changed accordingly and the Second Edition part was left off of the title.<br /> <br /> So TLDR, the God-Machine Chronicle is the name of the campaign setting that was used to sell Second Edition before it was called Second Edition.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-03-2017, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T20:10:25-08:00","id":1057905,"title":"","content":"Spoiled for discussion of the writing process of this section. I'm specifically talking about the history of the &quot;Voice of an Angel&quot; piece of fiction, because it's an important part of the meta-game answer of what the God-Machine Chronicle is that Charlaquin doesn't explain. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I would add that the God-Machine began as simply the Voice of an Angel, which was the first piece of fiction at the beginning of the first edition World of Darkness book. The piece became very popular amongst readers and writers both, so the writers began dropping references scattered throughout different books to something called the God-Machine. When the time came to do an updated rule-set, they wanted to give an example mystery, as an 'example chronicle' of sorts. The first edition base book really only had Ghosts if i remember correctly, but it had this fantastic piece of fluff. Additionally, the idea of the God-Machine offered the opportunity to do a novel take on Demons as a playable splat, so they began working on the Demon: the Descent and the God-Machine Chronicles side-by-side.<br /> <br /> What this most notably means for you, though, is that the Voice of an Angel was written YEARS before anything else in the God-Machine Chronicle, and is included to show the inspiration for the rest of the chronicle, and as an in-world document, and as you've already noted in a few places, is contradicted in quite a few ways by other portions of the text, including the actual game mechanics, such as the ephemera bit with the blood you noted. (Though Angels CAN have blood in some circumstances, it's really quite complicated).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which reminds me, also linking into the past discussion on what books you should read, you should very much consider reading the fiction anthologies. I only have the God-Machine Anthology, but it's fantastic writing, and I think you'd very much enjoy it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, this is currently my favourite thread on this website, I love reading along with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","user":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","date":". 03-03-2017, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:35:04-08:00","id":1058176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057819#post1057819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a Clarke's Third Law thing. It can't violate the laws of physics, but its understanding of the laws of physics are sufficiently advanced to the point where it can do things that might <i>look like</i> violating those laws to us primitive humans.<br /> <br /> So yeah, now that you're here, I'm going to give the meta-game answer to what the God-Machine Chronicle is, because it's been driving me crazy waiting this long. I'll put it in spoiler tags for now, in case you want to finish the section before reading this, but I can't wait any longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small addition to what Charlaquin said there:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rich Thomas has gone on record saying that the death of the World of Darkness MMO had a lot to do with CCP letting him just call the Chronicle Books &quot;Second Editions&quot;. There was fear that there would be brand confusion between the MMO and the (then) World of Darkness TTRPG, because even though they share DNA, they're still ultimately different settings.<br /> <br /> The new IP owners had much the same fear, because they want to do transmedia stuff with the Classic WoD. That's why we now have CofD instead of nWoD. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:49:12-08:00","id":1058180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1058176#post1058176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Small addition to what Charlaquin said there:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rich Thomas has gone on record saying that the death of the World of Darkness MMO had a lot to do with CCP letting him just call the Chronicle Books &amp;quot;Second Editions&amp;quot;. There was fear that there would be brand confusion between the MMO and the (then) World of Darkness TTRPG, because even though they share DNA, they're still ultimately different settings.<br /> <br /> The new IP owners had much the same fear, because they want to do transmedia stuff with the Classic WoD. That's why we now have CofD instead of nWoD. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:51:40-08:00","id":1058219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing?p=1057770#post1057770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The optional rule about <b>Fate</b> doesn't really seem necessary to me. I think Aspirations are enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting sidenote: This system was actually cut from the original God-Machine update, but it inadvertently ended up back in the new core because of a slight editorial oversight. The developer decided it was easier (and more interesting) to just add it into that sidebar, rather than have to comb through the book all over again and remove it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian